IGI (d)IM-pì-lá-aḫ IGI en-um-a-šur DUMU PUZUR₄-a-šur,"Witnessed by Adad-pilah, witnessed by Ennam-Aššur son of Puzur-Aššur."
10 ma-na URUDU SIG₅ 0.83334 GÍN.TA 0.5 SÌLA Ì.GIŠ 1 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a šu-mì zu-ku-a e-pu-li,"10 minas of good copper at the rate of 0.83334 shekel, 0.5 litre of oil, and 1 shekel of silver he balanced for the sake of Zukuwa."
mì-ma a-nim i li-bi be-lúm-ba-ni DUMU a-šur-be-el-a-wa-tim a-lá-ḫu-um i-šu,All this Bēlum-bāni son of Aššur-bēl-awātim owes to Ali-ahum.
22 šu-ru-tum 11 ma-na 10 GÍN AN.NA 12 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ší-im 0.5 ku-ta-nim 2.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ší-im 5 ANŠE.ḪI.A i li-bi₄ a-lá-ḫi-im,"22 dark textiles, 11 minas 10 shekels of tin, 12 shekels of silver the price of 0.5 textile, and 2.5 minas of silver, the price of 5 donkeys, are due by Ali-ahum."
a-na 2 ANŠE.ḪI.A ša e-lá-ma ù lá-qé-ep a-lá-ḫu-um ù ḫi-na-a uk-ta-nu-ma,"Concerning 2 donkeys belonging to Elamma and Lā-qēp, Ali-ahum and Hinnaya will establish the facts."
a-šar i-bu-ru-ni 0.5 ma-na.TA KÙ.BABBAR e-la-ma ú la-qé-ep i-la-qé-ú,"Wherever they establish liability, Elamma and Lā-qēp will take 0.5 mina of silver each."
IGI e-dí-na-a IGI en-um-a-šùr,"Witnessed by Edinaya, witnessed by Ennam-Aššur."
