ṭup-pu-um ša ší-bu-tí-a ša IGI šu-ga-ri-a-im ša a-šùr,Tablet of my testimony before the šugarri'ā'um of Aššur.
wa-bar-tum ša ša-mu-ḫa i-dí-ni-ma ṭup-pá-am a-dí-in,"The station of Šamuha gave it to me, and I gave the tablet."
um-ma šu-ku-bu-um a-na a-šùr-DU₁₀ qí-bi₄-ma,Thus says Šu-Kūbum: say to Aššur-ṭāb.
mì-šu ša a-dí KÙ.BABBAR ta-áš-ta-na-pá-ra-ni,Why is it that you keep writing to me about the silver?
a-wa-tí-a a-šur-ma-lik ù kur-ub-IŠTAR ú-ga-me-ru-ma 3 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR i-nu-mì-šu-ma a-na kur-ub-IŠTAR áš-qúl,"Aššur-mālik and Kurub-Ištar have settled my case, and at that time I paid 3 minas of silver to Kurub-Ištar."
ší-tí KÙ.BABBAR a-na kur-ub-IŠTAR áš-qúl,The rest of the silver I have now paid to Kurub-Ištar.
ú a-dí ma-lá ú ší-ni-šu té-er-tí i-li-kà-kum a-na KÙ.BABBAR mì-ma lá ta-áš-ta-na-pá-ra-am,And as my instructions went to you twice: Do not keep writing to me at all about the silver!
a-bu-ša-lim mì-ma lá il₅-qé,Abu-šalim has taken nothing of it.
a-wa-tù-a IGI a-bu-ša-lim-ma i-gi₅-im-ra,My affairs were actually settled in the presence of Abu-šalim.
um-ma i-tur₄-DINGIR-ma a-na en-um-a-šùr qí-bi-ma,Thus says Itūr-ilī: say to Ennam-Aššur.
a-dí a-wa-tim ša a-bi-kà ša a-na be-el KÙ.BABBAR ú-ma-li-ú-ma ma-ga-ra-am lá i-mu-ú-ni-ni ú-ma-am a-wi-lu im-ta-ag-ru-ni,"As for the matter of your father, for which I paid the owners of the silver and they would not agree with me, today the men have agreed."
um-ma šu-nu-ma šu-pu-ur-ma me-er-ú a-we-lim li-li-ku-ni-ma a-li ús-ma-at-ni a-ta-ma mì-li-ik,"They said: Write so that the man's sons come here, and then you yourself decide what is fitting."
a-pu-tum KÙ.BABBAR 5 ma-na lá ús-ma-sà-a,Urgent! Is silver up to 5 minas not fitting?
ra-ma-ku-nu za-ki-a-ma al-kà-ni-ma a-wa-at-ku-nu le-qé-a-ni,"Clear yourselves, come here and take up your matter."
1 GÚ URUDU ma-sí-am ša É ša-ni-a-am SIG₅ x ša x x ù ḫa-ra-ni-a šé-bi₄-lam-ma,"Send me 1 talent of washed copper of the second house, of good quality, for my journey."
ma mì x ma-na.TA URUDU ú e-li-iš ša 10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR URUDU ma-as-a-am le-qé-a-ma,And take washed copper for 10 minas of silver at the rate of x minas of copper or higher.
tí-ir-ta-kà li-li-kam-ma KÙ.BABBAR a-na-kam lá-áš-qú-ul ú ANŠE lu-šé-ri-a-kum,Let your report come to me so I may pay the silver here and I shall send a donkey to you.
1 ma-na 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a-šur-DU₁₀ DUMU a-zu-za-a ḫa-bu-lam,Aššur-ṭāb son of Azuzaya owes me 1 mina 10 shekels of silver.
ṭup-pu-šu ḫa-ar-ma-am ú-kà-al,I hold his certified tablet.
KÙ.BABBAR ma-lá KÙ.BABBAR i-tù-wa-ar,The silver will return in full.
šu-ma a-ma-i lu-qú-sú a KÙ.BABBAR i-da-ma ḫa-ra-an sú-ki-ni-ma i-ta-lá-ak,If Ama'ī sells his goods for silver and has departed on the narrow track.
2.33333 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR a-ta ú šu-ut ku-un-kà-ma a-ṣé-ri-a ú a-ṣé-er ša ki-ma šu-a-tí šé-bi₄-lá-nim,Then you and he seal 2.33333 minas of silver and send it to me and to his representative.
GAN-lam a šu-m,It should pass overland in his name.
um-ma ma-ma-ḫi-ir ù SIG₅-pí-a-šur a-na a-lá-ḫi-im DUMU šál-ma-a-šur,Thus say Man-mahir and Damiq-pī-Aššur to Ali-ahum son of Šalim-Aššur.
1 DUG GIG 3 a-za-mì-lá-tum tí-ib-nim KI a-šur-ma-lik DUMU (d)a-šur-(d)UTU-ši,1 jar of wheat and 3 sacks of straw are with Aššur-malik son of Aššur-šamšī.
3 DUG GIG KI ša-pu-na-aḫ-šu,3 jars of wheat are with Šapunahšu.
2 DUG GIG KI wa-lá-a,2 jars of wheat are with Walā.
3 DUG ŠE-um KI wa-lá-ma,3 jars of barley are also with Walā.
1 DUG GIG KI wa-al-ku,1 jar of wheat is with Walku.
3 DUG GIG KI ḫu-da,3 jars of wheat are with Huda.
1 na-ru-uq 2 DUG ŠE-um KI i-na-ar DUMU e-lá-lí,1 sack and 2 jars of barley are with Inar son of Elālī.
1 na-ru-uq 3 DUG ŠE-um ŠÀ.BA 2 DUG ar-ša-tum KI du-nu-um-na ṣú-ḫa-ri-im ša ḫa-šu-i GAL re-i,"1 sack and 3 jars of barley, including 2 jars of wheat, are with Dunumna, the servant of Hašui the chief shepherd."
ŠU.NÍGIN 7 na-ru-uq lu ŠE-um lu ar-ša-tum,"Total: 7 sacks, whether barley or wheat."
iš-tí um-mì-iš-ḫa-ra ù en-um-a-šùr pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR ù šu-be-lúm i-mì-ig-ru-ma,Pilah-Ištar and Šu-Bēlum reached an agreement with Ummī-Išhara and Ennam-Aššur.
KÙ.BABBAR 6.66666 ma-na ša É ḫi-na-a 4 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša kur-ub-IŠTAR DUMU a-lá-ḫi-im ù i-na ku-ur-sí-nim ša IŠTAR-pì-lá-aḫ 1.3333300000000001 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR na-dí-šu-nu-tí,"6.66666 minas of silver of the house of Hinnaya, 4 minas of silver of Kurub-Ištar son of Ali-ahum, and 1.33333 mina of silver from the pot of Ištar-pilah have been deposited for them."
KÙ.BABBAR a-nàm pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR ù šu-be-lúm a-na um-mì-iš-ḫa-ra ù en-um-a-šur qá-sú-nu ik-bu-sú-ma ša-lá-áš šu-ba-tim qá-qí-ri ša 5-tum i-dí-nu-šu-nu-tí-ni,"Regarding this silver, Pilah-Ištar and Šu-Bēlum waived their claim in favor of Ummī-Išhara and Ennam-Aššur for 3 house-units of land which the committee of five had given them."
iš-tí um-mì-a-an e-lá-ma a-bi-šu-nu um-mì-iš-ḫa-ra ù en-um-a-šùr ú-bu-bu qá-qí-ri-šu-nu i-lá-qé-ú,"When Ummī-Išhara and Ennam-Aššur effectuate a clearance with the investors of their father Elamma, they will take their plot."
ITU.KAM té-i-na-tim li-mu-um en-na-sú-en₆ DUMU šu-a-šùr,"Month: Te'inātum, eponymy: Enna-Suen son of Šu-Aššur."
a-na 3 ša-na-tim qá-qí-ri-šu-nu ú-bu-bu-šu-nu-tí,They will effectuate the clearance of their plot for them within three years.
šu-ma lá ú-bi-bu-ú 3 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR i-na ša kur-ub-IŠTAR i-lá-qé-ú-ma,"If they fail to do so, they will take 3 minas of silver from that of Kurub-Ištar."
ší-im qá-qí-ri-šu-nu ušt-ta-bu-ú-ma a-na qá-qí-ri-šu-nu ù-lá i-tù-ru,They will be satisfied with the price of their plot and will not return to claim their plot.
i-na 3 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša kur-ub-IŠTAR qá-tí pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR ù šu-be-lim ša-ak-na-at,A claim of Pilah-Ištar and Šu-Bēlum rests upon the 3 minas of silver of Kurub-Ištar.
šu-ma té-bi-ib-tum i-tab-ší qá-dí a-ḫi-šun,"If a clearance occurs, they will be cleared along with their brothers."
2.83333 ma-na 7 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu-ki ša en-um-a-šur DUMU e-l␀-ṁma šu-sú-in DUMU ì-lí-a a-na lá-ma-sí-tim ù ir-ma-a-šur ip-qí-id-ma,2.83333 minas 7 shekels of silver under the seals of Ennam-Aššur son of Elamma and Šu-Suen son of Iliya he entrusted to Lamassītum and Ir'am-Aššur.
KÙ.BABBAR ir-ma-a-šur a-na a-lim(ki) a-šur ú-ba-al-šu,"Ir'am-Aššur will bring that silver to the City, Aššur."
a-na ḫu-bu-ul en-um-a-šur a-na DAM.GÀR i-ša-qal,He will pay it to the merchant for the debt of Ennam-Aššur.
KÙ.BABBAR a šu-mì en-um-a-šur GÁN-lam e-tí-iq,The silver will cross the territory in the name of Ennam-Aššur.
IGI pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR DUMU e-lá-ma IGI a-šur-ba-ni DUMU du-mu-uq-IŠTAR,"Witnessed by Pilah-Ištar son of Elamma, witnessed by Aššur-bāni son of Dumuq-Ištar."
a-na bu-ur-sú-in a-lá-ḫi-im a-lá-bi₄-ma ù ì-lí-mì-tí qí-bi₄-ma um-ma tám-kà-ru-ma,"To Būr-Suen, Alāhum, Alā-abum, and Ilī-imittī say: thus the merchant."
10 GÚ URUDU ma-sí-am 4 ANŠE ṣa-lá-mu ù 2 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ù a-ḫa-ma 0.66666 ma-na 2 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR be-ú-lá-at ṣú-ḫa-ri-im mì-ma a-ni-im bu-ur-sú-in a-lá-bu-um ù ì-lí-mì-tí na-áš-ú-ni-kum,"10 talents of washed copper, 4 black donkeys and 2 minas of silver, plus further 0.6666 mina 2 shekels of silver, the working-capital for the servant - Būr-Suen, Alī-abum and Ilī-imittī are bringing all this to you."
a-ḫi a-ta i-ḫi-id-ma URUDU a-na KÙ.BABBAR ta-e-ra-ma i-na ší-im URUDU ša ṣú-ḫa-ru i-qá-bi₄-ú-ni-ku-ni i-na ša-ḫa-tí-šú-nu i-zi-iz-ma ší-ma-am ša-ma-am,"My dear brother, take care to convert the copper into silver, and assist the servants with the proceeds from the copper which they mention to you, and then carry out a purchase."
1 ANŠE ṣa-lá-ma-am a-na-nu-um a-na šé-bu-lim le-qé-am,Take a black donkey from here for the shipment.
1.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu-ki-a bu-ur-sú-in ù ì-lí-mì-tí na-áš-ú-ni-kum,Būr-Suen and Ilī-imittī are bringing you 1.5 minas of silver under my seal.
KÙ.BABBAR-áp-kà le-qé-ma ṭup-pì li-it-a-ma a qá-tí bu-ur-sú-in ù ì-lí-mì-tí di-in,"Take your silver, cancel my tablet, and give it to Būr-Suen and Ilī-imittī."
a-ḫi a-ta lá i-sà-ri-ru ṭù-ur-da-nu-šú,"My dear brother, they should not delay; send them to me."
45 na-ru-uq ŠE-am x na-ru-uq ar-ša-tim a-ḫa-ma ša ša-da-aq-tí 45 na-ru-uq ŠE-am 5 na-ru-uq ar-ša-tum,"45 sacks of barley, x sacks of wheat; further, from last year, 45 sacks of barley and 5 sacks of wheat."
IGI ú-li-id ší-im-tám al-qé ki-ma ar-ša-tim ŠE-am al-qé,"In the presence of Ulid, I took the inheritance; I took barley instead of wheat."
i-nu-mì a-ḫu-wa-qar iš-tù a-lim(ki) i-tù-ra-ni šu-uq-lam ku-nu-ki ša a-lim(ki) xxx ù e-lá-ma i-pá-ṭù-ru-ma 50 ma-na AN.NA i-du-nu-šú-ma,"When Ahu-waqar returns from the City, [PN and] Elamma will open the packet with the seals of the City and they will give him 50 minas of tin."
iš-tù u₄-mì-im ša AN.NA i-lá-qé-ú 15 ḫa-am-ša-tim i-lá-ak-ma 8.33333 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am a-ḫu-wa-qar i-ša-qal,"From the day he receives the tin, fifteen weeks will pass and then Ahu-waqar will pay 8.3333 minas of refined silver."
11.5 ma-na URUDU ší-ku-um i-ṣé-er sú-kà-li-im lu-zi i-šu,Sukkallum owes 11.5 minas of šiku-copper to Luzi.
iš-tù ITU.1.KAM áb-ša-ra-ni li-mu-um ku-bi-a-a ki-ma a-wa-at kà-ri-im ṣí-ib-tam ú-ṣa-áb,"Reckoned from the month Ab-šarrāni, eponymy Kūbiya, he must add interest in accordance with the rule of the colony."
IGI ú-zu-a IGI i-dí-a-bi₄-im,"Witnessed by Uzuwa, by Iddin-abum."
2.33333 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am ku-nu-ki-a be-lá-lá-a ú-bi₄-il₅,Belalaya brought 2.3333 minas of refined silver under my seal.
3 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a qá-tí-šú a-dí-in,3 shekels of silver I gave him for expenses.
2 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a pá-ni-ri,2 shekels of silver for paniru-garments.
3.5 ma-na URUDU ša 4 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR sà-ḫe-er-tám,3.5 minas of copper with a value of 4 shekels of silver for small wares.
mì-ma a-ni-im xx ú a-šùr-mu-ta-pì-il₅ ub-lu,Aššur-mūtappil brought all this.
IGI (d)I-ba-ni DUMU ga-na-a IGI ku-lu-ma-a,"In the presence of Adad-bāni, son of Ganaya, and of Kulumaya."
a-šùr-i-mì-tí 0.33333 ma-na 5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN KÙ.GI a-ta-aḫ-šú ú-bi₄-il₅-šú-um,"As for Aššur-imittī, 25 shekels of silver and 1 shekel of gold Atahšu brought him."
a-na e-lá-ma qí-bi₄-ma um-ma a-šur-SIPA-ma,"Say to Elamma, thus Aššur-rē’ī:"
4 GÚ 20 ma-na AN.NA ku-nu-ki 1 me-at 21 TÚG mì-ma a-ni-im a-ra-de₈-a-kum,"4 talents and 20 minas of tin under seal and 121 textiles, all this I am leading to you."
um-ma kà-ru-um kà-ni-iš-ma a-na ša-qí-il₅ da-tim ší-ip-ri-ni kà-ar kà-ar-ma ú wa-bar-ra-tim qí-bi₄-ma,"Thus the colony of Kanesh: say to the payers of the datu-contribution, to our messengers, and to every colony and trading station:"
ṭup-pu-um ša a-lim(ki) i-li-kam,A letter of the City has arrived.
i-na ṭup-pì-im ša a-lim(ki) iš-tù u₄-mì-im a-nim ma-ma-an KÙ.AN i-ša-ú-mu-ni i-na né-mè-lim da-šùr ú-lá e-WA iš-ra-tí-šú kà-ru-um kà-ni-iš i-lá-qé,"In the letter of the City (it says): from this day on, whoever buys amūtu-iron, (the City of) Aššur will not share in the profit; the colony of Kanesh will collect the tithe of it."
ki-ma ṭup-pì-ni ta-áš-me-a-ni a-ma-kam lu a-na ší-mì-im a-na É.GAL-lim i-dí-in lu té-ra-at É.GAL-lim ú-kà-lim lu na-ší-ma a-dí-ni lá i-dí-in ma-lá KÙ.AN na-áš-ú ni-bi₄-it a-ší-im šu-um-šú ú šu-mì a-bi₄-šú i-na ṭup-pì-im lu-up-ta-nim-ma iš-tí ší-ip-ri-ni šé-bi₄-lá-nim,"As soon as you have heard our letter, whoever there has either sold it to a palace, or has offered it to palace officials, or still carries it with him without having yet sold it - for all the amūtu-iron he carries, write the exact amount of every piece, his name and his father's name on a tablet and send it here with our messenger."
me-ḫe-er ṭup-pì-ni a-na kà-ar kà-ar-ma ú wa-bar-ra-tim šé-bi₄-lá,Send a copy of this letter of ours to every colony and to all the trading stations.
KÙ.AN lu a-na DAM.GÀR-ru-tim i-dí-in šu-mì a-wi-lim lu-up-ta-nim,"Even when somebody has sold amūtu-iron via a trading agent, register the name of that man."
um-ma en-na-num-ma a-na id-na-a ù a-šur-… qí-bi-ma,Thus Ennānum: say to Idnaya and Aššur-...:
a ma-lá áš-pu-ra-ku-nu-tí-ni a-na tí-ir-tí-a ša x x im … i-ra-dí-ú a-pu-tum i-ḫi-id-ma ki-ma ša qá-qí-dí-kà lu-qú-tí ù e-ma-ri-a a ma-lá a-wi-lu-tí-kà ša-ṣí-ir,"In accordance with what I wrote to you, regarding my orders that ... leads - urgent, pay attention and guard my goods and my donkeys like your own life as you are a gentleman."
i-nu-mì a-šur-i-mì-tí a-na a-lim(ki) i-li-ku KÙ.BABBAR 2 ma-na ú 3 ma-na a-na ra-mì-ni-šú na-ší,"When Aššur-imittī went to the City, he brought some 2 or 3 minas of silver on his own."
ù i-na a-lim(ki) 0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR bé-ú-lá-at ḫa-al-gi-a-šú a-šur-i-mì-tí il₅-qé,"And in the City, Aššur-imittī took 0.5 mina of silver, the working capital of Halgiaššu."
ma-lá ṣú-ba-tí ù AN.NA a-na ra-mì-ni-šú na-áš-ú za-ki-ma iš-tí-šú li-ib-ší,Clear whatever textiles and tin he brings on his own and let it remain with him.
tí-ir-ta-kà li-li-kam,Send me your report.
ú x x a ma-lá tí-ir-tí-a ša áš-pu-ra-ku-nu-tí-ni ep-ša,"Also, carry out ... in accordance with my instructions that I sent to you."
ù ṣí-ba-tim ša a-šur-i-mì-tí mì-ma lá i-sà-li-ma li-bi₄ lá i-ma-ra-ṣa-kum,"Also, with respect to the matters of Aššur-imittī, he must not lie, lest I become angry with you."
[...] a-na na-áp-ṭá-ar ku-pá-im i-ša-qú-lu,... they are to pay at the melting of the snow.
a-ḫa-ma 4.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR i-na li-bi wa-al-di-lim i-na e-ra-bi-šú-ma ú-šé-ba-lam [...] sú-kà-li-a,"Furthermore, he will send 4.5 shekels of silver from the assets of Wald-Ilim upon his arrival ... my messenger."
3.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR-áp ú-zu-a i-na li-bi-a ḫi-na-a il₅-qé,Hinnāya took 3.5 minas of Uzua's silver at my expense.
IGI a-šur-be-el-a-wa-tim DUMU šu-a-nim IGI en-nam-(d)IŠKUR DUMU zi-ra,"In the presence of Aššur-bēl-awātim son of Šu-Anum, and of Ennam-Adad son of Zira."
um-mì-a-nu-šú a-na ší-a-ma-tim ú-ra-ki-sú-ni,His investors had contractually bound me for making purchases.
um-ma i-na-a-ma a-na a-šur-DU₁₀ ú MAN-a-šur qí-bi-ma,From Innaya to Aššur-ṭāb and Puzur-Aššur: Speak!
a-na-kam ru-ba-um ù ru-ba-tum a-na ḫa-ra-na-tim ša pá-zu-ur-tim iš-pu-ru-ma,The king and queen here have written to the road-guards concerning smuggling.
um-ma šu-nu-ma ša i ma-tim TÚG.ḪI.A ù AN.NA na-áš-ú ma ta-ma ra ni ṣa-áb-ta-ma AN.NA ú TÚG.ḪI.A a-tù-nu kà-i-lá-ma ra-ga am i-a-tí ri-id-a-am,"They said: ""Seize anyone you observe carrying textiles and tin in the land, and then withhold the tin and textiles and lead the criminal to me."""
ú a-na ša ḫa-ra-an sú-ki-nim iš-ta-áp-ru,"Also, they have written to those of the Narrow Track."
a-pu-tum AN.NA ù TÚG.ḪI.A lá tù-pá-za-ra,Urgent: do not smuggle tin and textiles.
ú a-na ḫa-ra-an sú-ki-nim mì-ma lá ta-ša-kà-na,And do not commit anything to the Narrow Track.
