ša 2.75 (TÚG)ku-ta-nim 0.83333 ma-na 5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR i-na ILLAT-at en-um-a-šùr DUMU ba-sá-sá ù (d)en-LÍL-ba-ni i-na É.GAL-lim e-lá-ma a-dí-im,"For 2 3/4 kutānu-textiles Elamma is entitled to 55 shekels of silver in the palace from the caravan of Ennam-Aššur, son of Basasa, and from Enlil-bāni."
a-bu-ni i-na bu-ul-ṭí-šu 9 TÚG.ḪI.A a-na be-et kà-ri-im na-dí,Our father deposited 9 textiles at the office of the colony while he was alive.
