KÙ.BABBAR u KÙ.GI i-a-um,that silver and gold belong to me!
ṭuppam ša šībē ša bāb ilim ša KÙ.BABBAR u KÙ.GI šīāūni tukallimī-ma,"A tablet by witnesses, drawn up in the Gate of the God, to the effect that the silver and gold belong to her she showed me."
2 mana KÙ.BABBAR IGI Anuppiya DUMU Uṣur-ša-Aššur IGI Urad-Aššur DUMU Watrim IGI Aššur-nīšum DUMU Izkanim IGI,"and 2 minas of silver, in the presence of Anuppiya, son of Usur-sa-Assur, of Urad-Assur, son of Watrum, of Assur-nisu, son of IZkanum, I gave her."
umma Šalim-Aššur-ma ana Ennam-Aššur u Ali-ahim qibī-ma,From Šalim-Aššur to Ennam-Aššur and Ali-ahum:
KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN bulāṭūni malā amakam ibaššiū lu KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN ša libbika u libbi Ali-ahim ul naṭū-ma ana ālim ul nišamma,"As for every shekel of silver of our funds as much as is there, as well as every shekel of silver in your possession and in Ali-ahum's - it is not a good idea for us to send it to the City."
... KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN ul ēli ul ana ṣibtim nidaššū-ma KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN ēli ana nakam šīāmātum-ma,"Either a single shekel will accrue, or we should give every shekel of silver as interest-bearing loans, so a profit of some shekels of silver will accrue."
1.33333 mana 5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN pahhirā-ma anakam ...,Here purchases are possible and of 1.3333 mina 5 shekels of silver... Collect every shekel of silver so here...
KÙ.BABBAR 10 mana ... ta-du-nu,at least 10 minas of silver ...
ana Ennam-Aššur qibī-ma lu AN.NA lu ṣubātū malā eliūnikkuni ana šīāmātim ibašši,"To Ennam-Aššur: Tin as well as textiles, what accrues to you is available for purchases."
1 (TÚG) ṣubātum ša ibaššiū ana Ali-ahim u Aluwa dīn-ma lublūnim,Every textile that is available give that to Ali-ahum and Aluwa so they may bring it.
ana dāš'išu bā'ānim,Leave in the spring.
lu ištēniūtū-ma KÙ.BABBAR lu šīm husāri lu šīm ṣubātī ... tērtakunu lillik-ma KÙ.BABBAR ...,"May for the very first time the silver, the proceeds from the lapis lazuli or from the textiles... send me word."
62 ku-ta-ni a-na ir-i-bi-im ù šé-ep-IŠTAR e-zi-ib,I left 62 kutānus with Ir'ibum and Šēp-Ištar.
ŠÀ.BA 30 ku-ta-ni a-na šu-pu-nu-ma-an ni-dī-in,We gave thereof 30 kutānus to Šuppunuman.
5 TÚG a-na ra-dī-im iš-bi-a-ni-tī-im,5 textiles for the guide from Išhianit.
11 ku-ta-ni i-na na-ru-qá-tim du-ur-kà-ma a-šu-mì da-dí-a e-ez-ba,Pack 11 kutānus in the sacks and leave them in Dādiya's name.
a-dí tí-ir-tí i-lá-kà-ni ši-tí ku-ta-ni-a 16 TÚG i-ši-tù-nim,until my instructions arrive. The rest of my kutānus - 16 textiles remain.
wa-ar-ki-a-ma a-na ši-tí-im ma-lá ta-du-nu-šu-ni a-ṣé-ri-a šé-bi-lá-šu-nu,"After I left, with respect to the remainder, send me as much as you will sell."
1.5 GÍN AN.NA i-na a-al bu-u-na-tim a 	É wa-áb-ri a-dí-in,1.5 shekel of tin in the town of Buṭātum I gave to the inn.
6 GÍN AN.NA i-na pá-ṭí ša Ḧa-na-ak-na-ak a-šar ni-IS-GA-ru a-na É ub-ri a-dí-in,"6 shekels of tin in the area of Hanaknak, where we..., I gave to the inn."
3 GÍN AN.NA i-na Ḧa-ni-ga wa-ṣa-i-ni a-na É ub-ri a-dí-in,"3 shekels of tin, when we left Hanigga, I gave to the inn."
3 GÍN AN.NA i-na wa-zi-da a-na É ub-ri a-dí-in,3 shekels of tin I gave in Wazida to the inn.
6 GÍN AN.NA a-na ni-is-Ḧba-tim ša TÚG.ḦI.A i-na Ḧa-na-ak-na-ak a-dí-in,6 shekels of tin I gave in Hanaknak as import-tax on the textiles.
14 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ší-im áš-qúl,14 shekels of silver as price I paid.
3 GÍN AN.NA iš-tù Ḧa-na-ak-na-ak i-wa-ṣa-i-a a-na É ub-ri-ni a-dí Ḧu-lu-qá-e ni-iš-e-ú a-dí-in,"3 shekels of tin, when I left Hanaknak I gave to our inn, while we searched for goods lost."
3 GÍN AN.NA i-na a-al ku-pì-il₅-ša-an a-dí-in,3 shekels of tin I gave in the town of Kupilšan.
1.5 GÍN AN.NA i-na ta-pá-kà-áš a kà-ší-im a-dí-in,1.5 shekel of tin I gave in Tapaggaš to the chief.
Ḧi-dam AN.NA a-na a-lá-Ḧbi-nim ša ta-e-dí-zi-na a-dí-in,A bead of tin I gave to the steward of Ta'edizina.
0.5 ma-na URUDU a-né-bar-tim i-ša dur₄-Ḧbu-mì-it a-dí-in,0.5 mina of copper I gave for the crossing in the area of Durhumit.
3 ma-na URUDU SIG₅ ni-is-Ḧba-tim i-na dur₄-Ḧbu-mì-it a kà-ší-im a-dí-in,"3 minas of refined copper, import-tax, in Durhumit I gave to the chief."
5 ma-na URUDU SIG₅ i-nu-mì a-na wa-aḦ-šu-ša-na ur-ki TÚG.ḦI.A i-li-ku a qá-tí ì-lí-úṣ-ra-ni a-dí-in,"5 minas of refined copper I put at the disposal of Ilī-uṣranni, when he went to Wahšušana in pursuit of my textiles."
10 ma-na URUDU ší-kam lu a É ub-ri lu gám-ri i-na wa-aḦ-šu-ša-na,10 minas of copper for the inn and expenses in Wahšušana.
50 NINDA i li-bi₄ a-lá-Ḧbi-nim ša-áp-li-im ša tù-um-li-a,50 loaves of bread owed by the lower miller of Tumliya.
ki-ma NINDA 1 DUG ar-ša-tim i-da-nam,"Instead of bread, he shall give 1 jar of wheat."
4 GÚ AN.NA ku-nu-ki ša a-šùr-i-mì-tí (d)IM-ba-ni ir-dí-a-ni,"4 talents of sealed tin of Aššur-imittī, Adad-bāni brought to me."
nu-sà-ni-iq-šu-ma 4 GÚ 6 ma-na 5 GÍN AN.NA ni-is-ni-iq,We checked it and we checked 4 talents 6 minas 5 shekels of tin.
ŠÀ.BA 0.83333 ma-na ni-is-Ḧba-at AN.NA-ki-šu a-na É kà-ri-im ni-dí-in,"From it, we gave 5/6 mina as the import-tax of his tin to the office of the colony."
IGI en-na-a-šùr DUMU a-ni-nim,Witnessed by Enna-Aššur son of Anninum.
IGI en-um-a-šùr DUMU ú-zu-a,Witnessed by Ennum-Aššur son of Uzua.
ŠÀ.BA AN.NA 2 GÚ 2 0.5 ma-na ša-lim-a-šùr il₅-qé,"From that tin, Šalim-Aššur took 2 talents 2.5 minas."
41 ma-na 11.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am ku-nu-ki ša ki-ma šu-a-tí ú ku-nu-ki-a 3 né-pí-šu a-Ḧba-ma,"41 minas 11.5 shekels of refined silver, sealed by his representatives and by me - in 3 packages; further."
0.66666 ma-na 1 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša-du-a-sú mì-ma a-nim a-na šu-nu-nu ù ì-lí-áš-ra-ni áp-qí-id-ma a-ṣé-er ša-lim-a-šur a-na a-lim(ki) ub-lu,"0.6666 mina 1 shekel of silver, its transport tariff - all this I entrusted to Šu-Nūnu and Ilī-ašrannī, and they brought it to Šalim-Aššur in the City."
a-Ḧba-ma 5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a-na ú-ku-ul-tí-šu-nu a-dí-šu-nu-tí,"Furthermore, I gave them 5 shekels of silver for their food."
IGI a-Ḧbu-wa-qar DUMU šu-IŠTAR IGI ba-zi-a DUMU DINGIR-ku-ru-ub IGI a-šur-ta-ak-lá-ku DUMU qàr-da-a,"Witnessed by Ahu-waqar son of Šu-Ištar, by Baziya son of Ilī-kurub, by Aššur-taklāku son of Qardaya."
a-Ḧba-ma 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a be-a-li-im a-na šu-nu-nu,"Furthermore, I gave 10 shekels of silver as a working-capital to Šu-Nūnu."
7 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a-na ì-lí-áš-ra-ni ma-aḦá-ri-šu-nu-ma a-dí-in,And 7 shekels of silver to Ilī-ašrannī witnessed by the same men.
KIŠIB sú-en-na-da DUMU e-nam-a-šùr,Seal of Suen-nādā son of Ennam-Aššur.
a-na a-wa-tim a-ni-a-tim kà-ru-um kà-ni-iš i-dí-ni-ma IGI GÍR ša a-šùr ší-bu-tí a-dí-in,The Kanesh colony gave me for these proceedings and I gave my testimony before Aššur's dagger.
šu-ku-bu-um DUMU a-šur-i-dí ù i-dí-IŠTAR DUMU a-šur-na-da tap-pá-ú-a,Šu-Kūbum son of Aššur-idī and Iddin-Ištar son of Aššur-nādā were my (absent) partners.
0.5 ma-na 7 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ú 2.25 GÍN KÙ.GI IŠTAR-lá-ma-sí DAM ku-ni-li a-na lá-ma-sà-tim DAM e-lá-ma té-zi-ib,"37 shekels of silver and 2 1/4 shekels of gold Ištar-lamassī, wife of Kū-ilum, left to Lamassutum, wife of Elamma."
KÙ.BABBAR ú KÙ.KI a-na en-nam-a-šur DUMU a-šùr-dan ú šu-mì-a-bi₄-a DUMU a-mu-a lá-ma-sà-tum DAM e-lá-ma x ú en-nam-a-šur DUMU e-lá-ma i ša-Ḧba-at um-mì-šu i-zi-iz-ma ip-qí-du,"That silver and gold Lamassutum, wife of Elamma, attended by Elamma's son Ennam-Aššur, entrusted to Ennam-Aššur, son of Aššur-dān, and Šumi-abiya, son of Amua."
IGI PÚZUR-a-šur DUMU i-ku-pí-a IGI a-mur-DINGIR DUMU šu-ku-bi-im IGI ma-ṣí-ì-lí DUMU bu-zu-zu IGI PÚZUR.IŠTAR DUMU šu-ku-bi-im,"In the presence of Puzur-Aššur, son of Ikū-pīya, of Amur-ilī, son of Šu-Kūbum, of Maṣi-ilī, son of Buzuzu, of Puzur-Ištar, son of Šu-Kūbum."
a-na en-na-nim DUMU a-bi₄-a ú a-lá-Ḧba-im DUMU šál-ma-a-šùr,To Ennānum son of Abiya and Ali-ahum son of Šalim-Aššur.
KIŠIB PUZUR₄-a-šur,Seal of Puzur-Aššur.
13.33333 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am i-ṣé-er i-dí-a-bi₄-im a-mur-IŠTAR i-šu,Iddin-abum owes 13.3333 minas of refined silver to Amur-Ištar.
IGI a-šur-e-mu-qí IGI en-nam-a-šur DUMU me-na-a,"Witnessed by Aššur-emūqi, by Ennam-Aššur son of Menaya."
25 áb-na-tum iš-tí e-na-aḦba-DINGIR,25 stones owed by Enah-ilī.
40 áb-na-tum iš-tí ku-ša-ra-a,40 stones owed by Kušaraya.
a-na en-nam-a-šur qí-bi-ma um-ma a-lá-Ḧba-um-ma,To Ennam-Aššur from Ali-ahum.
a-Ḧba-i a-ta a-ma-kam iš-tù a-wa-tù-um i-ba-tù-qú-ni tí-ir-ta-kà li-li-kam-ma a ma-lá tí-ir-tí-kà le-pu-uš,"My dear brother, send me word there after the matter has been dropped, then I shall act in accordance with your instructions."
a-ṣé-er ANŠE a-ni-ú-tim 3 ANŠE ù ṣú-Ḧba-ri šé-ri-a,Dispatch 3 donkeys and servants in addition to these donkeys.
a ma-lá té-er-tí-kà le-pu-uš,I shall act in accordance with your instructions.
a-al-DU₁₀ a-na a-mur-a-šur iṣ-ba-at-ni-a-tí-ma um-ma a-al-DU₁₀-ma a-na a-mur-a-šur-ma,Āl-ṭāb seized us against Amur-Aššur and Āl-ṭāb said to Amur-Aššur:
KÙ.BABBAR a-ta ù šu-IŠTAR mì-iš-lá ša-qá-lá-am lá qá-bi-a-tù-nu,"""Have you and Šu-Ištar not promised to pay each half of the silver?"
um-ma a-mur-a-šur-ma ke-na KÙ.BABBAR mì-iš-lá ša-qá-lá-am qá-bi-a-ni-ma,"Amur-Aššur answered: ""True, we have promised to pay each half of the silver"
ù i-né-ma-li ša-li-iš-tám ša-tim áš-du-na-da i-zu-a-az,and also that he would receive as a share one third of the profit
ù a-na i-bi-sà-e ša-li-iš-tám i-za-az,"and that he also would be responsible for one third of the losses""."
IGI a-ta-tí-a IGI a-ḥu-wa-qar IGI a-šur-(d)UTU,"In the presence of Atatiya, of Ahu-waqar, of Aššur-šamšī."
a-šu-mì sú-bi-ri-im ša ip-ṭí-re,"Concerning the Subaraean, of the ransom."
Ṭup-pu-um ša 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša be-ú-lá-at a-bu-ša-lim DUMU PÚZUR.IŠTAR,"A tablet about 10 shekels of silver, the working capital of Abu-šalim, son of Puzur-Ištar;"
Ṭup-pu-um ša ku-nu-uk PÚZUR-a-šur a-na 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR lá i-tù-ar,"a tablet with Puzur-Aššur's seal, he will not come back on 10 shekels of silver;"
Ṭup-pu-um ša 0.33333 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša be-ú-lá-at a-bi-a-a DUMU ú-zu-a,"a tablet about 0.3333 mina of silver, the working capital of Abiaya, son of Uzua;"
Ṭup-pu-um ša 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša DINGIR-ma-lik DUMU a-de₈-lá-at,"a tablet about 10 shekels of silver of Ilī-mālik, son of Adad-ellat;"
Ṭup-pu-um ša 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša i-na-sú-in DUMU za-ar-ni-qí-im ša be-ú-lá-tí-šu,"a tablet about 10 shekels of silver of Ennam-Suen, son of Zarniqum, of his working capital;"
ù Ṭup-pu-um ša 13.16666 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša e-nam-sú-in DUMU a-lá-bi-im,"and a tablet of 13.1666 shekel of silver of Ennam-Suen, son of Ali-abum;"
Ṭup-pu-um ša 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša lá-qí-pí-im DUMU a-gu₅-a,"a tablet about 10 shekels of silver of Laqēpum, son of Agua;"
na-áš-pè-er-tum ša a-lá-ḥi-im ù DUMU ku-zi-zi-a,a letter of Ali-ahum and the son of Kuziziya;
Ṭup-pu-um ša 0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša šu-ma-a,a tablet of 0.5 mina of silver of Šumaya.
ŠU.NÍGIN 9 Ṭup-pu-ú i-na ta-ma-lá-ki-im ša i-ša-sú-ú ta-ba-ku-tum,"In all 9 tablets in a tablet box, to be read and thrown away."
a-na a-lá-ḥi-im ù i-ku-pí-a-šùr qí-bi₄-ma um-ma za-li-dí-ma,To Ali-ahum and Ikūn-pī-Aššur from Zalidi:
0.83333 ma-na 3 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am ù 0.5 ma-na a-ḥa-ma a-mu-ra-am a-na šu-a-šùr DUMU i-dí-a-šùr ḥa-bu-lá-ku,I owe 53 shekels of refined silver plus a further 0.5 mina of checked silver to Šu-Aššur son of Iddin-Aššur.
Ṭup-pá-am ša 4 x ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša DAM.GÀR xx-ma a-na a-bi₄-ni ḥa-bu-lu a-na ša-pár-tim ú-kà-al,"The tablet concerning 4 minas of silver which the agent owes to our father, he holds as security."
be-lí a-ta KÙ.BABBAR a-na šu-a-šùr šu-qú-ul-ma Ṭup-pì šé-ṣí-ma iš-tí-kà li-ib-ší-ú,"My dear lord, pay the silver to Šu-Aššur, get out my tablet and let it be with you."
ù té-er-ta-kà li-li-kam-ma lá-at-bi₄-a-ma lá-tal-kam,"Also, send me word so I can set out and leave."
ù a-dí Ṭup-pì-im ša (d)UTU-ba-ni a-dí ma-lá ù ší-ni-šu ni-gi₅-ri-ma,"Also, with respect to Šamaš-bāni's tablet we sued both once and twice,"
ša ki-ma ku-a-tí Ṭup-pá-am ta-da-nam lá i-mu-ú,but your representatives refuse to give the tablet.
té-er-ta-kà a-ṣé-er ša ki-ma,Send word to your representatives.
1 ma-na 14 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ni-is-ḥa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu,"1 mina 14 shekels of silver, the excise on it extra, the transport fee for it paid;"
a-ḥa-ma 0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ni-is-ḥa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu ik-ri-bu ku-nu-ki ša DAM.GÀR,"separately 0.5 mina of silver, the excise on it extra, the transport fee for it paid, temple funds, under the seals of the agent,"
en-um-a-šur a-na ir-ma-a-šur ip-qí-id-ma a-na a-lim(ki) a-na ší-a-ma-tim ú-bi-il₅,Ennam-Aššur entrusted to Ir'am-Aššur and he brought it to the City for making purchases.
IGI a-zu-ta-a DUMU e-me-me IGI ì-dí-ba-ni DUMU ir-ma-a-šur,"In the presence of Azutāya, son of Ememê, of Idi-bāni, son of Ir'am-Aššur."
3 na-áš-pè-ra-tum ša ku-nu-uk sà-ak-li-a x x a x x x UD i-na a-lim IGI ma-x-im IGI-x x-na ṭá-á-btim ša-ak-na,3 missives sealed by Sakliya placed in the City with Ma... and others as witnesses.
i-na x x x za ḥa-x x bi … x ba-li x x x 0.16666 GÍN 1 x x x-ki a-ni áš-qú-ul,I paid 10 shekels of silver in the presence of witnesses.
KÙ.BABBAR ša um-ma-ša a-na me-er-i-tí-ša i ba-áb-tim té-zi-bu a-na ḥu-bu-ul a-na a-ḥe-ša a-tù-nu ta-lá-qé-a,"The silver that her mother left to her daughter as part of the outstanding claims, do you want to take it for the debt, for her brothers?"
ni-zi-iz-ma i-na a-wa-tim ni-bu-šu-nu-ma iš-tù gám-ru-um,We took action and rebutted them by our argumentation.
ù ša a-na bi-ki-tim ša um-mì-ki ù a-ḥi-ki iṣ-ḥe-ru ší-tí KÙ.BABBAR 0.5 ma-na 7 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ù 2.25 GÍN KÙ.GI,"After the expenses made for the bewailing of your mother and your brothers had been deducted, the rest of the silver was 37 shekels of silver and 2 1/4 shekels of gold,"
ku-nu-ki ša en-um-a-šùr ù šu-mì-a-bi-a a-na en-um-DINGIR DUMU ḥa-da-a i-na pu-ùḥ-ri-ni ni-ip-qí-id-ma na-áš-a-ki-im,"under the seals of Ennam-Aššur and Šumi-abiya we together entrusted to Ennam-ilī, the son of Hadāya, and he is on his way to you with it."
i-na ŠÀ.BA KÙ.BABBAR ri-ik-sí-im 2.25 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša ì-lí-a ni-is-ḥa-tum ša a-šùr na-ad-a,"In the packet of silver 2 1/4 shekels of silver of Iliya, excise for Aššur, have been put."
KÙ.BABBAR šu-a-tí a-na É li-mì-im dí-ni,Give that silver to the office of the limmum.
KÙ.BABBAR a-ni-um É e-lá-ma ib-ší,This silver was in Elamma's house.
2 ṣí-il₅-a-nu ša ṭup-pé-e ku-nu-ku ša a-ḥe-ki ù um-mì-ki i-ba-ší-ú,There are still two containers with tablets sealed by your brothers and mother.
pá-al-ḥa-ni-ma pá-ṭá-ra-am ú-lá ni-mu-wa,We did not dare to open them because we were afraid.
lá ta-áš-ta-na-me-i ki-ma um-mì-ki iš-tù 10 ša-na-tim nu-a-um aḥ-zu-ma i-na É nu-a-im wa-áš-ba-at-ni,Have you not heard that the Anatolian is since ten years married to your mother and that she lived in the house of the Anatolian?
a-na KÙ.BABBAR ma-dí-im mì-ma lá ta-da-gi₅-li,"Do by no means expect much silver,"
KÙ.BABBAR a-mì-um ù KI-kam um-mì-ki,there is only the afore-mentioned silver and the seal of your mother.
iš-tù ḥa-mu-uš-tim ša a-lá-ḥi-im ù bu-sí-a i-ša na-ra-am-ZU ù i-ku-nim KÙ.BABBAR ni-iš-qúl,Reckoned from the week eponymy of Ali-ahum and Buṣiya we paid the silver during that of Naram-Suen and Ikūnum.
15 ma-na URUDU ma-sí-a-am i-na áb-na-tí-ni i-na ṣé-er ú-na-bi₄ ù a-ší-a-at lu-zi i-šu,"Unabi and Ašiat owe 15 minas of washed copper, weighed with our stones, to Luzi."
iš-tù ḥa-mu-uš-tim ša a-mu-ru-um-ba-ni ú a-šur-na-da a-na 4 ḥa-am-ša-tim i-ša-qú-lu,Reckoned from the week of Amurrum-bāni and Aššur-nādā they must pay within 4 weeks.
šu-ma lá iš-qú-lu ki-ma a-wa-at kà-ri-im ṣí-ib-tám ú-ṣú-bu,"If they have not paid in time, they must add interest according to the rule of the colony."
i-na pu-ru-uš-ḥa-dim URUDU-am i-ša-qú-lu,They must pay the copper in Purušhaddum.
ITU.KAM ḥu-bu-ur li-mu-um i-dí-a-bu-um,"Month Hubur, eponymy Iddin-abum."
IGI i-dí-a-bi₄-im DUMU i-tur₄-DINGIR,Witnessed by Iddin-abum son of Itūr-ilī.
a-na a-lá-ḥi-im qí-bi-ma um-ma zu-ku-a-ma,To Ali-ahum from Zukuwa:
lá-ma a-li-kà-ni AN.NA-kà ta-dí-in,Before I came your tin was sold.
šu-qú-ul-tí AN.NA-ki-kà 1 GÚ 30 ma-na 0.5 ma-na mu-ṭá-e i-šku-nu,The weight of your tin was 1 talent 30 minas; 0.5 mina they established as losses.
ša ki-ma ku-a-tí áš-a-al-ma um-ma a-na-ku-ma ke-e AN.NA ta-dí-na-šu,"I questioned your representatives, saying: ""How did you sell the tin?"""
um-ma šu-nu-ma 8 LÁ 22.5 ŠE GÍN.TA ta-dí-in,"They answered: ""It was sold at the rate 8 minus 22.5 grains."""
KÙ.BABBAR-áp-šu ṣa-ba-at-ma 11.33333 ma-na 2 GÍN ší-tí an-ni-ki-kà,"Seize the silver, 11 1/3 minas 2 shekels was the rest for your tin."
lá-ma a-li-kà-ni KÙ.BABBAR lá ta-áš-qú-ul,Before I arrived you had not been paid the silver;
iš-tù u₄-mì-im ša a-li-kà-ni KÙ.BABBAR ú-ša-áš-qí-il₅-ma KÙ.BABBAR i ku-nu-ki-ni i-ba-ší,the day I arrived I had the silver paid and the silver is under our seals.
ki-ma i-na a-li-ki DUMU um-me-a-nim ša KÙ.BABBAR 10 ma-na na-áš-ú lá-šu-ma a ší-a-tí KÙ.BABBAR ni-ik-lá,"Since there is no affiliated trader among the travellers who can be responsible for some 10 minas of silver, for that reason we held the silver back."
li-ba-kà mì-ma lá tù-la-ma-an,Do not get angry.
KÙ.BABBAR na-dí,The silver is ready.
a-dí 5 u₄-me-e šu-ḥu-bur wa-ṣa-a-am qá-bi,Within 5 days Šu-Hubur has promised to leave.
iš-tí šu-ḥu-bur KÙ.BABBAR-áp-kà nu-šé-ba-lá-kum,We shall send you your silver with Šu-Hubur.
i-na ša ṭup-pí-šu ḥa-ar-mì-im šu-ku-tám 4 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ú-ša-áš-qí-il₅-šu-ma,I made Šukkutum pay 4 minas of silver from what was in his certified tablet.
ŠU.NÍGIN KÙ.BABBAR-pí-kà x lu ší-im AN.NA xxxxx we-du-um xxxxx ša šu-ki-tim iš-té-ni-iš 15 ma-na 11 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu,"Total of your silver, from the proceeds of the tin and from Šukkutum, in all Šu-Hubur will bring you 15 minas 11 shekels under our seals."
um-ma kà-ru-um kà-ni-iš-ma a-na a-li-ki qí-bi-ma,"Thus the Kanesh colony, say to the travelers:"
a-na-kam sú-en₆-SIG₅ im-ḥu-ur-ni-a-tí-ma um-ma šu-ut-ma,Here Suen-damiq has appealed to us and he said:
li-ip-ta-num DUMU qar-da-a ú-ta-ra-am a-na ta-ú-ri-šu ma-aṣ-a-ku,"""I want Liptānum, son of Qardaya, to be brought back; I take responsibility for bringing him back""."
DU₁₀-ṣí-lá-a-šùr ší-pár-ni,Ṭāb-ṣilli-Aššur is our messenger.
iš-tí DU₁₀-ṣí-lá-a-šùr li-tù-ra-am,He must come back with Ṭāb-ṣilli-Aššur.
a-tù-nu lu e-mu-uq-šu,You must be his executive force.
a-na ì-lí-e-mu-qí šu-ta-mu-zi a-bi₄-a-a e-lá-a ù lá-ma-sí qí-bi-ma um-ma a-dí-da ù a-lá-hu-um-ma,"To Ilī-emūqī, Šu-Tammuzi, Abiya, Elaya and Lamassī from Adida and Ali-ahum:"
iš-tù ša-lim-a-šur me-tù-ú DAM.GÀR-ru-ú ša a-bi₄-ni ša a-ma-kam KÙ.BABBAR ša ha-bu-lu-ni i-a-tí ù en-um-a-šur lá-am-ni-iš e-pu-šu-ni-a-tí-ma sí-ku-ni ù ba-a-ba-tù-ni ṣa-bu-ta-ma a-tù-nu ta-áš-me-a-ma a-na a-lim(ki) ta-lí-kà-ma a-lu-um dí-nam i-dí-in-ma um-ma,"After Šalim-Aššur died, our father's customers to whom he owed silver there treated me and Ennam-Aššur badly, we were detained and our outstanding claims blocked, and you heard about it and went to the City assembly, and the City gave a verdict as follows:"
šu-ma KÙ.BABBAR ša-lim-a-šur i-na eq-lim ha-bu-ul i-na tup-pì-šu ù ší-bi₄-šu i-ku-an-ma i-na sá-bi-tí-šu KÙ.BABBAR-áp-šu i-lá-qé,"if Šalim-Aššur owed silver abroad, it must be proved with his tablet and witnesses and he (the creditor) may then receive his silver from the funds available;"
a-na hu-bu-ul ša-lim-a-šur ša i-na a-lim(ki) ha-bu-lu ma-ma-an KÙ.BABBAR i-na eq-lim lá i-lá-qé,"as for the debt that Šalim-Aššur owed in the City, noone could take any silver abroad."
ma-ma-an ša il₅-qé-ú ú-ta-ar,Whoever took any would have to return it;
ša lá ú-ta-e-ru i-ša-ri-iq-šum,who did not return it would have it taken away by force.
…-me-er … … …-ku-nim-ma … … šu a-lam ha x lu … li-mu-um ni-ta šu ma mì … ša-lim-a-šur 3 x x x x x x x i-za-zu a-na a-lim x ta-lí-kà-ni,... the eponym ... Šalim-Aššur ... they will stand ... To the City ... when you went to the City...
me-eḥ-ra-at tup-pì-im ša a-lim(ki) a-ba-ba ra-bi₄-ṣú-um ub-lá-ma KÙ.BABBAR ša ṣa-bu-tù ú-šé-ru-ma sí-ki-ni ú-kà,"Ababa, the attorney brought a copy of the tablet of the City and they released all the silver that had been confiscated, but they detained us."
2 GÚ 10 ma-na AN.NA ku-nu-ki 52 TÚG SIG₅ 3 ANŠE.HI.A ṣá-lá-mu ku-nu-ki ša a-šùr-ba-ni ù be-lúm-ba-ni ša tám-kà-ri-im a-na PUZUR₄-a-x ip-qí-du,"2 talents 10 minas of sealed tin, 52 good textiles, 3 black donkeys, sealed by Aššur-bāni and Bēlum-bāni and belonging to a merchant, they entrusted to Puzur-A..."
lu-qú-tám a-ni-tám PUZUR₄-a-… a-na a-lá-hi-im ip-qí-id,Puzur-A... entrusted these goods to Ali-ahum.
IGI a-šùr-ba-ni DUMU ku-ta-a IGI SIG₅-pí-a-šùr DUMU ÌR-ad-ì-lí-šu DUMU a-šùr-i-dí,"Witnessed by Aššur-bāni son of Kutaya, by Damiq-pī-Aššur son of Warad-ilīšu, (grand)son of Aššur-idī."
a-na ú-ṣur-ša-IŠTAR ù a-šur-ba-ni qí-bi-ma um-ma a-lá-hu-um-ma,To Uṣur-ša-Ištar and Aššur-bāni from Ali-ahum:
it-qú-ra-am ša Ì.GIŠ il₅-pu-tù-ku-nu-ni ta-al-qé-a,You have taken the spoon with which they anointed you with oil.
it-qú-ru-um 0.5 GÍN URUDU lá tù-ba-al,"The spoon is not worth 0.5 shekel of copper,"
ki-ma KÙ.BABBAR 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ù 0.33333 ma-na li-bi-i im-ta-ra-aṣ,but I became upset as if it was worth 10 or 20 shekels of silver.
a-ma-kam a-na ú-ṣur-ša-IŠTAR dí-ší-ma a-na am-tim li-dí-ší,Give it to Uṣur-ša-Ištar there so he can give it to the maid.
šu-ma lá ta-dí-in-ší li-bi₄ i-ma-ra-aṣ,"If you have not give it, I shall be upset."
a-na 5-ší-šu šé-né-en na-áš-ú-ni-kum,... they bring you for 5 pairs of shoes.
šu-be-lam tùr-dam,Send me Šu-Bēlum.
4 GÚ AN.NA ù it-ra-sú ku-nu-ki ša a-lim(ki),"4 talents of tin plus its extras, sealed in the City,"
20 ku-ta-ni qá-dum 12 ku-ta-ni ma-ṭí-ú-tim ša li-wi-tim a-ha-ma 20 ku-ta-ni qá-tám ša e-kál-lúm a-na ší-mì-im il₅-qé-ú a-na qá-tí ša-lim-a-šùr ṭá-ah-ú,"20 textiles including 12 of low quality for wrapping, further, 20 textiles, the share that the palace took for pre-emption, have been transferred to Šalim-Aššur's account -"
ŠU.NÍGIN 40 ku-ta-ni ù 5 ANŠE.HI.A ṣá-lá-me i-na lu-qú-tim ša šé-ep šu-ku-bi-im i-li-kà-ni ša-lim-a-šùr il₅-qé,in all Šalim-Aššur has received 40 textiles and 5 black donkeys from the merchandise that arrived with Šu-Kūbum's transport.
ší-tí ṣú-ba-tí-šu 45 ku-ta-nu qá-du-um ṣú-ba-tí-šu SIG₅ ku-nu-ku ša šu-ku-bi-im É ša-lim-a-šùr i-ba-ší-ú,"The rest of his textiles, 45 including his textiles of good quality, are in Šalim-Aššur's house under Šu-Kūbum's seal."
3 ku-ta-ni ni-is-ha-tim e-kál-lúm il₅-qé,The palace received 3 textiles as import duty;
3 ku-ta-ni ša li-wi-tim SIG₅ e-kál-lúm il₅-qé ù 2 ku-ta-nu i-na e-kál-lim iḥ-li-qú,"the palace received 3 from the wrapping of good quality, and 2 were lost in the palace."
15 ma-na AN.NA a-ṣé-er AN.NA-ak qá-tí-šu ša šu-ku-bi-im a-na ni-ip-lá-tí-šu a-na ša-lim-a-šùr iš-qú,Šu-Kūbum has paid 15 minas of tin on top of his expense tin as balance to Šalim-Aššur.
IGI (d)MAR.TU-ba-ni DUMU ma-na-na IGI PUZUR₄-a-na DUMU i-dí-(d)IM,"Witnessed by Amurrum-bāni son of Manana, by Puzur-Anna son of Iddin-Adad."
ni-kà-sú ša iš-ra-tim ša É kà-ri-im a-dí-ni ú-lá ša-sí-ú,The accounts concerning the tithe concerning the office of the colony have not yet been settled.
a-na ša-lim-a-šùr qí-bi-ma um-ma šu-(d)DUMU.ZI a-dí-da e-lá-a ù la-ma-sí-ma,"To Šalim-Aššur from Šu-Tammuzi, Adida, Elaya and Lamassī:"
i-na wa-ṣa-i-kà … um-ma a-ta-ma a-šùr-DU₁₀ DUMU lu-lu KÙ.BABBAR 10 ma-na,When you left ... you said: Lulu's son Aššur-ṭāb ... at least 10 minas of silver ...
iš-ra-tí-šu ru-ba-um i-lá-qé,the king will receive its / his tithe.
i-na wa-ar-ki-tim a-we-lu-um a-na a-lim(ki) i-li-ik-ma um-ma šu-ut-ma a-na ší-a-ma-tim i-dí-nam,"Later the man went to the City assembly and said: ""He gave it to me for purchases."""
qí-ip-tám a-dí 5 ša-na-tim qé-pá-ku,"""I was entrusted with a credit for 5 years."""
iš-tí a-lim(ki) e-na-na-tim e-ri-iš-ma u₄-me-šu a-dí ša-na-at ša ki-ma šu-a-tí ú-ša-za-az-ma … ša ki-ma šu-a-tí uš-… lu qí-ip-tám ta-qí-pu,"He asked for a favour from the City assembly, and his representative will set his terms for a year and ... his representative ... whether you entrusted on credit ..."
a-na en-um-a-šur qí-bi-ma um-ma lá-qé-ep-ma en-na-nu-um ú a-na-ku a-na hu-ur-ší-kà né-ru-ma,To Ennam-Aššur from Lā-qēp: Ennānum and I entered your storeroom and
tup-pì-kà ú ší-pá-ri-kà nu-šé-ṣí-ma i-na É i-tur₄-DINGIR né-zi-ib,brought out your tablets and your bronze (objects) and left them in Itūr-ilī's house.
1.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ú 3 GÍN 22.5 ŠE KÙ.GI ša iš-tù kà-tí-lá e-ra-mu-ša ub-lá-ni,1.5 mina of silver and 3 shekels 22.5 grains of gold that Ewarimuša brought from Katila
i-na qá-qí-dim ša a-bi₄-kà en-na-aḥ-ì-lí ú a-na KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu-ki-kà ni-x-ma 1.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ni-il₅-pu-ut,"from the capital of your father Enah-ilī, also for the silver under your seal, we have ... and we have booked 1.5 mina of silver."
3 ṣú-ub-ru-um ša a-na ša-lim-bé-li ta-dí-nu-ni ŠÀ.BA 1 ṣú-ub-ru-um a-šu-mì kà-tí-lá-i-im kà-tí,"As to the three slaves that you gave to Šalim-bēlī, of them one slave has been taken as security because of the man of Katila."
ú-mu-um li-ṭí-bu-ma ra-dí-a-am iš-tí na-gi-ir a-lim le-ri-iš-ma a-ma-at-kà i-ta-ru-ú-ni,(When) the weather improves let him ask for a guide from the town herald so they will bring along your maid.
1 ṣú-ba-ar-kà i ha-ra-nim me-et,Your one slave died on the road.
ṣú-ub-ra-am i-na ha-ra-nim a-na 0.33333 ma-na 4 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR i-dí-šu,He sold a slave on the road for 24 shekels of silver.
4 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR i li-bi₄ ša-lim-bé-li a-hu-ur,4 shekels remain in Šalim-bēlī's possession.
ša 1.8333300000000001 ma-na 2 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR.BE 8.75 GÍN ni-iš-a-ma-ku-um,"For 1.83333 mina 2 shekels (of tin), in silver 8 3/4 shekels, we bought it for you."
16 ma-na AN.NA na-áš-ú-ni-kum,They bring you 16 minas of tin.
a-ha-ma 0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ú 4 na-ru-uq ar-ša-tum ga-me-er,"Further, 0.5 mina of silver and 4 sacks of wheat have been spent."
um-ma ma-ma-hi-ir-ma a-na a-lá-hi-im qí-bi₄-ma,From Man-mahir to Ali-ahum: Inform me
šu-ma TÚG.HI.A ša lu-hu-za-tí-a ú-šé-ri-bu-nim lá ú-šé-ri-bu-nim úz-ni pè-té,whether or not they have brought in the textiles from Luhuzattiya.
šu-ma ú-šé-ri-bu-ni-šu-nu a ma-lá ú-ša-hi-zu-kà a-na KÙ.BABBAR ta-er-šu-nu,"If they have brought them in, then convert them to silver as I instructed you."
a-bi a-ta i-hi-id-ma KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN šé-li-am,"My dear brother, take care to raise every shekel of silver."
pá-zu-ur-ta-šu-nu 7.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR,Smuggling them cost 7.5 shekels of silver.
0.66666 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR iš-tí en-na-sú-in e-ri-šu-ma 7.5 GÍN d-šu-nu-tí,They asked for 0.6666 minas of silver from Enna-Suen but give them 7.5 shekels.
ší-tí KÙ.BABBAR iš-tí-kà li-ib-ší,Let the rest of the silver be with you.
KIŠIB zu-ba DUMU en-na-nim KIŠIB PUZUR₄-a-na DUMU a-šur-dan KIŠIB na-áb-sú-in DUMU PUZUR₄-we-er KIŠIB a-al-DU₁₀,"Seal of Zuba son of Ennānum, seal of Puzur-Anna son of Aššur-dan, seal of Nab-Suen son of Puzur-Wer, seal of Al-ṭāb."
ša 11 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR qá-ta-at a-al-DU₁₀ a-šur-(d)UTU ú en-na-sú-in il₅-ta-ap-tù-ni,"The guarantees of Al-ṭāb, Aššur-šamšī, and Enna-Suen for the 11 minas of silver have been recorded."
šu-ma KÙ i-na ṣé-er a-šur-(d)UTU ú en-na-sú-in i-ta-al-qé É-bé-tum ša a-lim(ki) ša a-al-DU₁₀ e-ru-ba-at KÙ,"If silver is taken from Aššur-šamšī and Enna-Suen, the house of Al-ṭāb's daughter in the City will be the security for the silver."
5 ma-na … KÙ.BABBAR ša-du-a-sú ša-bu,"5 minas ... of silver, its transport tariff paid,"
ku-nu-ki-a ú ku-nu-ki ša be-lá-nim a-na DINGIR-pì-lá-ah áp-qí-id,under my seal and the seal of Bēlānum I entrusted to Ilī-pilah.
KÙ.BABBAR ša hu-ni-a IGI da-da-a DUMU a-šùr-i-mì-tí IGI e-lá-lí DUMU ga-UR-wa-a IGI a-šùr-lá-ma-sí DUMU šu-ku-bi₄-im,"Silver of Huniya. Witnessed by Dadaya son of Aššur-imittī, by Elālī son of Gawurwaya, by Aššur-lamassī son of Šu-Kūbum."
0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR i-ṣé-er a-zu a-lá-ḫu-um i-šu,Azu owes 0.5 mina of silver to Ali-ahum.
5 na-ru-uq ŠE-am 5 na-ru-uq ar-ša-tim 2 UDU.ḪI.A ù 20 NINDA ṣí-ba-at KÙ.BABBAR-pì-im,"5 sacks of barley, 5 sacks of wheat, 2 sheep and 20 loaves of bread are the interest on the silver."
ù KÙ.BABBAR a-na ḫa-ar-pé-e ú-ba-lá-am,the silver itself he will bring by harvest.
IGI ga-al-ga-li-a IGI ša-ra-ak-šu-na,"Witnessed by Galgaliya, by Šarakšuna."
KIŠIB bé-lí-a DUMU DINGIR-kur-ub,Seal of Bēlīya son of Ilī-kurub.
KIŠIB ša-lim-a-šur DUMU (d)IM.SIG₅,Seal of Šalim-Aššur son of Adad-damiq.
KIŠIB a-lá-ḫi-im DUMU šu-ku-bi-im,Seal of Ali-ahum son of Šu-Kūbum.
KIŠIB DU₁₀-pí-a-šùr DUMU a-lá-ḫi-im,Seal of Ṭāb-pī-Aššur son of Ali-ahum.
KIŠIB (d)UTU-a-bi DUMU sú-sà-nim,Seal of Šamaš-abī son of Sūsānum.
2 GÚ URUDU ma-sí-am ša DU₁₀-pí-a-šùr ki-ma (d)UTU-a-bi a-na lu-zi i-dí-nu-ma ù ṭup-pá-am ša lu-zi DU₁₀-pí-a-šur iḫ-ri-mu,"As to the 2 talents of washed copper that Ṭāb-pī-Aššur gave to Luzi on behalf of Šamaš-abī, and for which Ṭāb-pī-Aššur certified a tablet for Luzi:"
um-ma DU₁₀-pí-a-šùr-ma šu-ma URUDU i-na kà-ni-iš(ki) (d)UTU-a-bi ša ki-ma ku-a-tí il₅-qé-ú a-na 1 GÚ URUDU ma-sí-im ša tal-qé-ú 2 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ta-ša-qal,"Ṭāb-pī-Aššur said: ""If your representatives have received the copper in Kanesh from Šamaš-abī, you must pay 2 minas of silver for every talent of washed copper."""
DU₁₀-pí-a-šur ù (d)UTU-a-bi ša-bu-ú,Ṭāb-pī-Aššur and Šamaš-abī have been satisfied.
ṭup-pu-um ša 2 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša ta-ar-ki-is-tí lu-zi ša e-li-a-ni sà-ar,Any tablet concerning 2 minas of silver from the contract of Luzi that may appear will be invalid.
a-na ú-ṣú-ra-nim ù en-nam-a-šur qí-bi-ma,To Uṣurānum and Ennam-Aššur say:
um-ma IŠTAR-ra-bi₄-at-ma,thus says Ištar-rabiʾat;
a-na en-nam-a-šur qí-bi₄-ma,specifically to Ennam-Aššur:
a ma-lá tí-ir-tí-kà ša a-lu-wa ta-áš-pu-ra-ni wa-ar-ḫa-am iš-té-en ù 2 wa-ra-am e-ri-iš-kà-ma lá ta-áš-me-a-ni,"In accordance with your message which you sent with Aluwa, I asked you for one or two months, but you did not listen to me."
KÙ.BABBAR 2 ma-na i-na be-et DAM.GÀR-ri-im a-sí-ma,I have borrowed 2 minas of silver in a merchant-house.
ù i-na IGI me-ra um-me-a-nim KÙ.BABBAR i ku-nu-uk a-lu-wa kà-ni-ik-ma i-na be-tí-a-ma i-ba-ší,"And with an affiliated trader as witness, the silver was sealed with Aluwa's seal, and it is in my own house."
me-er-i a-ta,"My dear son,"
lu ṭup-pu-um ša ḫu-bu-ul ṣí-lá-(d)IM lu ṭup-pu-um iš-té-en ù ší-na lu ṭup-pu-um ša be-lu-ba-ni i-ba-ší,"the tablet concerning Ṣill-Adad's debt as well as one or two other tablets, and the tablet concerning Bēlum-bāni are available."
a-ma-kam IGI ú-ṣú-ra-nim ṭup-pì a-na pu-zu-ur-ku-nu ù a-lu-wa pí-iq-dá-ma lu-ub-lu-nim,Entrust those tablets there with Uṣurānum as witness to Puzurkunu and Aluwa so they may bring them.
a-na i-tur₄-DINGIR ù a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma,To Itūr-ilī and Ali-ahum say:
um-ma i-na-sú-in-ma,thus says Enna-Suen:
a-ša-me-ma en-nam-a-šur me-et,I hear that Ennam-Aššur is dead.
17 GÚ URUDU SIG₅ ḫa-bu-lam,He owes me 17 talents of copper of good quality.
a-na a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi₄-ma,To Ali-ahum say:
ṭup-pì-a ta-ma-lá-kam ku-nu-ki-a IGI šu-be-lim DUMU ku-zi-zi-a IGI šu-IŠTAR DUMU šu-ki-tim e-zi-ba-kum,"I left you my tablets, a container under my seal, with Šu-Bēlum son of Kuziziya and Šu-Ištar son of Šukkutum as witnesses."
um-ma a-na-ku-ma,I said:
šu-ma ma-ma-an i-na DAM.GÀR-ri lu KÙ.BABBAR lu URUDU ú-šé-ba-lam mu-ḫu-ur-ma ṭup-pì-a šé-ṣí-a-ma,"If any of the customers sends either silver or copper, receive it and take out my tablets."
a-šar KÙ.BABBAR-pì lá i-ḫa-li-qú e-pu-uš,Act so that my silver is not lost.
2 ma-na KÙ.GI a-na a-mur-(d)UTU ša-áp-kà-ku,I have invested 2 minas of gold in Amur-Šamaš.
1 ma-na KÙ.GI a-na a-lá-ḫi-im DUMU sí-ku-ḫi-im ša-áp-kà-ku,I have invested 1 mina of gold in Ali-ahum son of Sikuhum.
1 ma-na KÙ.GI a-na a-zu-za ša-áp-kà-ku,I have invested 1 mina of gold in Azuza.
