ù ku-kà-ni-na-am ša ki-ra-nim mì-da-tim i-na ku-nu-ki-šu PUZUR₄-a-mu-ri-ma ik-nu-uk-ší,And Puzur-Amurrum himself sealed the kukanninu-containers for the wine measures with his seal.
IGI e-ni-ša-ri-im ú IGI a-lu-wa ša i-zi-zu-ni,Before Enišarru and before Aluwa who were present.
2 GÚ 16 ma-na AN.NA ku-nu-ki-a ù a-ha-ma 10.33333 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša ik-ri-be ša a-šùr 2 ANŠE ṣa-lá-ma-an ù u₄-nu-sú-nu 1 ku-ta-num SIG₅ ša ša-tí-li mì-ma a-nim ša zu-ku-a,"2 talents 16 minas of tin under my seal plus further 10.3333 minas of silver from the votive offering to Aššur, 2 black donkeys and their harness, 1 good kutanu-cloth belonging to Šāt-ilī - all this belonging to Zukuwa."
a-ṣé-er ša ki-ma i-a-tí šu-hu-bur DUMU šál-ma-(d)IM da-da-a-a DUMU a-šùr-ba-ni ù a-šùr-ša-dí-li DUMU ì-lí-a-lim a-šùr-ša-dí-lí-ma ú-bi₄-il₅,"Aššur-šād-ilī brought (all this) to my representatives Šu-hubur son of Šalim-Adad, Dadaya son of Aššur-bāni and Aššur-šād-ilī son of Ilī-alūm."
um-ma a-na-ku-ma a-na ša ki-ma i-a-tí,I said to my representatives:
