5 ku-ta-ni a-na ha-ra-ni-a al-qé,I took 5 kutānu-textiles for my journey.
6 ku-ta-ni a-na-kam e-zi-ib,I left 6 kutānu-textiles here.
1 ku-ta-nam a-na 13 GÍN en-na-nu-um,Ennānum (took) 1 kutānu-textile for 13 shekels.
um-ma ku-zi-zi-a-ma ù a-mur-IŠTAR-ma a-na a-la-hi-im qí-bi-ma,Thus say Kuziziya and Amur-Ištar: say to Ali-ahum:
TÚG.HI-tù-kà i-na ma-ri-it-hi-im x SIG₅ i la xxxx-kam TÚG ra-qá-tum x ša ta-da-nim i-ni-id-nu,"Your textiles in Marithum, fine and thin textiles that have been sold, we gave."
ší-tí TÚG.HI-tí-kà i-ba-ší-ú,The rest of your textiles are available.
ší-mu-um kà-sí-i,The trade is at a standstill.
a ma-lá tí-ir-tí-kà TÚG.HI-tí-kà a-na ba-tí-iq ù DIRI ni-da-an-ma,In accordance with your instructions we shall sell your textiles for the best available price.
ù-ul KÙ.BABBAR-áp-šu ù-ul KÙ.GI-sú né-pá-ša-kum,And we shall make for you either silver or gold.
Ṭup-pu-ú ha-ru-mu-tum ša ší-bi-a ša me-er-e i-dí-a-bi₄-im,Certified tablets with my witnesses concerning the sons of Iddin-abum.
a-na en-na-nim ù a-lá-hi-im qí-bi₄-ma um-ma PUZUR₄-a-šùr-ma,To Ennānum and Ali-ahum from Puzur-Aššur:
20 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu-ki-a en-na-num na-ší,Ennānum brings 20 minas of silver under my seal.
KÙ.BABBAR i-na ma-na-i-šu áš-du a-na e-na-ah-DINGIR i-ta-ší-a-ma ṭup-pá-am ša ku-nu-ki-a li-dí-na-ku-nu-tí,"Ašdu weighed the silver with his weight for Enah-ilī, so let him give you a tablet with my seal."
ki-lá-lá-ku-nu-ma li-tí-a-šu-ma,Both of you should split the envelope.
ri-hi ù tù-ra-ma ku-un-kà-šu-ma a-šar a-šùr-ni-im-ri e-ez-ba-šu,... and seal it again and leave it for Aššur-nimrī.
ki-ma KÙ.BABBAR ta-áš-qú-lá-ni ma-ri-a-am ṭù-ur-da-nim,"When you have weighed the silver, send me the silver."
ù tí-ir-ta-ak-nu iš-tí pá-ni-e-ma a-li-ki li-li-kam,"Also, let your report come with the first transport."
a-hu-ú-a a-tù-nu ih-da mì-ma i-ṣé-ri-a ṣí-ib-tum lá i-lá-qé,"My dear brothers, take care so he does not take any interest from me."
a-na-kam a-na AN.NA ša KÙ.BABBAR 1 ma-na ú-šé-lá-šum,I shall realise every mina of silver on the tin here for him.
um-ma i-tur₄-DINGIR-ma a-na en-um-a-šùr qí-bi-ma,From Itūr-ilī to Ennam-Aššur:
lá li-bi₄ DINGIR-ma a-bu-kà me-et,"Sadly, your father has died."
x x x-bi-šu ṭup-pá-am x x x x bi-ki-tám x x x x an x x x x na x x hu x da x x ṣé-er-… x x tí … x x a-bi-… iš-tí ik … a-wa-tum lá ta-ga-…,... a tablet ... the mourning ... the words ... 
bu-lá-tù ša a-bi₄-kà kà-an-ku-ma i-ba-ší-ú,The assets of your father have been sealed and are available.
mì-ma ba-áb-tám i É-tim lá i-ba-ší-ú,There is nothing from outstanding claims in the house.
a-wa-sú iq-bi,He spoke his will.
um-mì-a-nu mu-ut a-bi₄-kà iš-me-ú-ma x a ta bu,The investors heard of your father's death and ...
a-na a-wa-tim ša i-pá-na nu-sá-li-ú-šù-nu-tí-ni a-wi-lu ma-ag-ru,The men agreed to that which we had earlier pleaded with them about.
a-pu-tum bu-lá-tim ša a-bi₄-ku-nu a-na KÙ.BABBAR … na ki-ma … …-šù-nu e-pu …,Urgent: (turn) the assets of your father into silver.
a-na-ku dam-qá-tim a-šé-e-a-kum,"While I am bent on doing what is good for you,"
a-ta lam-ni-iš té-pu-uš-a-ni,you have treated me badly.
x ta-ṣa-ba-at ù i-a-tí be-li ki-ma NINDA e-kà-lá-ni,"You have seized ... As for me, my lord is consuming me like bread."
ki-ma a-ma-kam tù-ša-zi-zi-ni um-ma a-ta-ma ší-im am-tim a-na me-er-i-a lá ta-dí-ni,"As you instructed me there, saying: 'You must not give the price of the slave-girl to my son!'"
a-na ší-a-tí a-na me-er-i-kà lá a-dí-ší,For that reason I have not given her to your son.
ší-im URUDU ù KÙ.BABBAR ba-áb-tám ša nu-a-am ú-ša-zi-za-ku-ni šé-bi₄-lam-ma ù šu-up-ra-am-ma a-ma-at-kà a-ša ki-ma ku-a-tí lá-dí-in,Send me the price of the copper and the outstanding silver for which I made the native responsible to you and send me a message then I will give your slave-girl to your representative.
1 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR i-ṣé-er a-li-li ù kà-ar-ší-ni wa-al-dí-lúm ù IŠTAR-lá-ma-sí i-šu-ú,Alili and Karšini owe 1 mina of silver to Waldi-ilum and Ištar-lamassī.
a-na ša tù-ùh-tù-ha-nim 1.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ù 2 UDU.HI.A i-du-nu,They will give 1.5 mina of silver plus 2 sheep for the feast of Tuhtuhānum.
IGI bé-li-kà-ù bé-el-tí-kà,Before your lord and your lady.
IGI wa-al-dí-lim ù kà-ar-ni-kà-šu,Witnessed by Waldi-ilum and Karnikašu.
a-na ša-lim-a-šùr qí-bi-ma um-ma (d)IM.GAL-ma,To Šalim-Aššur from Adad-rabi:
a-na ṭup-pí a-šu-mì i-dí-a-bi-im ša ta-áš-pu-ra-ni a-šùr-ma-lik ù ša-lim-a-šur áš-al-ma um-ma a-na-ku-ma,"As to the tablets concerning Iddin-abum that you wrote to me about - I asked Aššur-malik and Šalim-Aššur, saying:"
i-nu-mì i-sú-ri-ik a-wa-tim ša i-dí-a-bi-im iš-tí me-ra-ni iš-tí GUDU₄ ša IŠTAR ù É za-ak-ta-a ù a-li ta-ad-mì-iq-tám i-dí-nu-šù-ni a-wa-tim ig-mu-ru,"When Issu-arik cleared up Iddin-abum's affairs with Merani, with the priest of Ištar and Zaktaya's firm, and where he gave him a free loan, at that time they finished the matters."
i-nu-mì-šù-ma KÙ.BABBAR ša ša-qá-lim iš-qú-ul ù ší-tí KÙ.BABBAR ṭup-pí-šu ú-ha-ri-mu ša i-dí-a-bu-um ha-bu-lu-ma šál-ma-a-šùr qá-ta-tù-ni,"At that time he paid the silver for paying, but did they certify his tablets for the rest of the silver, stating that Iddin-abum owed it, and that Šalim-Aššur was the guarantor?"
um-ma šu-nu-ma ṭup-pu-um šu-um-šu ú-lá ha-ri-im,They answered: 'No tablet at all was certified.'
KÙ.BABBAR ú-šé-bi-lam-ma a-na a-wi-li ni-iš-qú-ul,He sent us the silver and we paid the men.
um-ma šu-nu-ma ke-na i-sú-ri-ik i-na ma-ah-ri-ni e-ta-wu-šù-um,They continued: 'It is true that Issu-arik discussed with him in our presence.'
um-ma šu-ut-ma ha-bu-ul a-hi-kà lu a-na-kam lu i-na GÁN-lim šu-qú-ul-ma ù a-lik-ma i-na KÙ.BABBAR-áp a-hi-kà le-qé,"He said: 'Pay the debt of your brother, both here and abroad, and then go and take it again out of your brother's silver.'"
šu-ma KÙ.BABBAR-áp a-hi-kà lá-šu i-na na-ru-qí-kà šu-qúl,"If there is no silver belonging to your brother, then pay out of your joint-stock capital."
a-na a-wa-tim a-ni-a-tim ša i-sú-ri-ik i-na ma-ah-ri-šù-nu e-ta-wu-ku-ni ú-šé-ra-sú-nu-ma KÁ DINGIR ṭup-pá-áš-nu a-lá-q,"For these words which Issu-arik discussed with you in their presence I shall lead them off, and I shall receive their tablet in the Gate of the God."
