0.33333 ma-na 1.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR i-ṣé-er ha-bi-a ù a-ší-tí-šu a-lā-hu-um i-šu,Habiya and his wife owe 0.3333 mina 1.5 shekel of silver to Ali-ahum.
um-ma e-lá-ma-ma ù kur-ub-IŠTAR-ma a-na da-da ù i-na-aḫ-DINGIR qí-bi-ma,"Thus Elamma and Kurub-Ištar, say to Dada and Ēnah-ilī:"
30 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša aḫ-ša-lim a-na a-bi-ku-nu ub-lá-ni šu-ma 15 GÍN.TA i-ba-ší AN.NA ša-ma-ma šé-bi-lá-nim,"The 30 minas of silver that Ah-šalim brought to your father, if there is tin available at a rate of 15 shekels (to 1), then buy it and send it to me."
šu-ma i-na 15 GÍN.TA ba-tí-iq mì-iš-lam AN.NA mì-iš-lam TÚG.ḪI.A ša-ma-ma i pá-ni-im-ma áb-kà-nim,If the rate is less than 15 shekels (to 1) then buy for one half of it tin and for the other half textiles and ship them to me with the first opportunity.
a-ni-ša-am a-ba-ra-im li-ik-šu-dam,It should reach me here before the suspension of traffic.
i-nu-mì AN.NA ù TÚG.ḪI.A ta-kà-na-kà i pá-ni šu-uq-lá-tim ù sí-ke TÚG.ḪI.A ša DAM.GÀR lá-pí-ta-nim,"When you seal the tin and the textiles write on the packets (with tin) and on the hem of the textiles: ""Belonging to the merchant""."
i ki-dim a-wa-at-ku-nu lá i-ša-me,No word of you should be heard outside!
KÙ.BABBAR ša e-la-ma,The silver belongs to Elamma.
