a-dí ITU.1.KAM iš-tí-in x x x x-ni šu x x x-ma a-ta-lá-kam,Within a single month ... I shall leave.
ú u₄-mu-a 2 ITU.KAM a-ḫu-ru,"Also, my term still runs for 2 months."
0.66666 ma-na 7.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am ki-iš-da-tí-a a-na i-dí-a-šùr DUMU dan-a-šùr i ra-mì-ni-a áš-qú-ul,"I myself paid 0.6666 mina 7.5 shekels of refined silver, my earnings, to Iddin-Aššur son of Dan-Aššur."
lu a-na ri-ig-ma-tim i-dí-a-šur ir-dí-ni-a-tí-ni lu a-na ṭup-pí ša ší-bi₄ i bá-áb DINGIR-lim ú-ga-ri-mu-ni 1 GÚ 40 ma-na ag-mu-ur-ma mì-iš-li-šu ṣí-li-a i-dín-nam,"I personally spent 1 talent 40 minas (of copper) both when Iddin-Aššur led us to the court case and when they produced the tablet with witnesses in the gate of the God, and Ṣilliya gave me half of that."
x 0.5 ma-na URUDU SIG₅ mu-ṣí-šu ú pu-ru-sà-e ša ra-bi₄-ṣí-im i ra-mì-ni-a áš-qú-ul,"I personally paid x 0.5 minas of good copper, the exit-tax and the decision of the attorney."
ú-ku-ul-tí MAŠKIM a-na-ku-ma ú-ša-qí-il₅,I too paid for the food of the attorney.
ṣí-li-a mì-ma a-na ú-ku-ul-tí-šu ú-lá i-dín,Ṣilliya did not give anything for his food.
i-nu-mì a-na-ku ù a-ba-ba a-ṣé-er ì-lí-dan e-tí-qú-ni i-na ḫa-ra-nim lu a-dí u₄-mì-im a-nim ni-is-ḫu-ru-ma a-wa-sú ni-ib-tù-qú-ni,"When I and Ababa travelled to Ilī-dan we were delayed on the journey until this very day, and we dropped his case;"
ú iš-tù ku-bu-ur-na-at a-dí dur₄-ḫu-mì-it ni-tù-ru-ni 0.5 ma-na 4 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ga-me-er,then we returned from Kuburnat to Durhumit - 0.5 mina 4 shekels of silver was the expense.
mì-ma a-nim a-dí a-wa-tim ša É a-bi-ni kà-šá-dim ú-ga-me-er,All this I have paid in order to conclude the matter of our father's house.
i-na KÙ.BABBAR ša É a-bi-a gám-ri a-lá-qé,I shall take my expenses from the silver of my father's house.
um-ma ša-lim-a-šur-ma sà-ba-sí-a ù tám-kà-ru-um-ma a-na pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR ù zi-ki-ki qí-bi-ma,"From Šalim-Aššur, Sabasiya and the merchant to Pilah-Ištar and Zikiki:"
30 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am ni-is-ḫa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu ša tám-kà-ri-im,"30 minas of refined silver, its import duty added, its transport tariff paid, belonging to a merchant;"
a-ḫa-ma 10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pu-um ni-is-ḫa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu ik-ri-bu ša a-šur ša tám-kà-ri-ma ku-nu-ki-šu a-na ṣé-er ì-lí-iš-tí-kál ù pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR zi-ki-ki na-áš-a-ku-nu-tí,"further, 10 minas of refined silver, its import duty added, its transport tariff paid, votive offerings for Aššur, also belonging to a merchant and sealed by him, Zikiki is bringing to you destined for Iliš-tikal and Pilah-Ištar."
a-na zi-ki-ki qí-bi-ma,To Zikiki:
a-ni-am a-na pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR pì-qí-id-ma iš-tí a-wi-tí-šu e-ta-wu ú a-ta i-na re-ší-šu i-zi-iz-ma KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN lu ṭá-ba-tí,Entrust this to Pilah-Ištar and join it to his consignment and then you personally may serve him and be positive over every shekel of silver.
a-na pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR qí-bi-ma,To Pilah-Ištar:
a-ḫu-ni a-ta li-bi₄ zi-ki-ki lá tù-lá-ma-an,"Our dear brother, do not make Zikiki angry."
ṭup-pè-en₆ ší-na ša a-ṣé-er ì-lí-iš-tí-kál ù pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR lá-pu-tù ša šé-ep zi-ki-ki iš-tí KÙ.BABBAR-ni x x-ba-šu-ni iš-tí pá-né-e-ma šé-bi₄-lá-ni-šu-nu,There are two tablets that were written to Iliš-tikal and Pilah-Ištar and that have been transported by Zikiki - send them together with our silver ... as soon as possible.
i-na ṭup-pè-en₆ a-me-e-en₆ qá-tum ša-kà-nu-um wa-du,Laying claim was indicated on those two tablets.
tí-ir-tí a-lim(ki) da-nu-tù-um i-li-kam,A strongly worded message from the City arrived.
qá-tum ša-kà-nu-um lá-šu,There is no way to lay claim.
we-da-ku,I am alone.
