KIŠIB šu-mì-a-bi-a DUMU zu-zu-ú KIŠIB lá-ba-na-da DUMU i-dí-sú-en₆ KIŠIB a-šùr-DU₁₀ DUMU e-na-ma-nim,"Seal of Šumi-abiya, son of Zuzū, seal of Labān-nādā, son of Iddin-Suen, seal of Aššur-ṭāb, son of Ennamānum."
1 GÚ AN.NA ku-nu-ki ša a-lim(ki) i-ṣé-er a-šur-DU₁₀ a-ḫu-qar i-šu,"1 talent of tin with seals of the city, Aššur-ṭāb owes to Ahu-waqar."
i-tù-a-ar DINGIR-šu-GAL ṣú-ḫa-ri-im ša a-šur-DU₁₀ iš-tù a-lim(ki) i-na ri-i-iš AN.NA 5 GÚ URUDU SIG₅ ma-sí-am ša-bu-ra-am a-na a-šur-DU₁₀ a-ḫu-qar i-ša-qal,"When Ilšu-rabi, the servant of Aššur-ṭāb, returns from the city, immediately when he receives the tin, 5 talents of refined copper of good quality, in pieces, Ahu-waqar will pay to Aššur-ṭāb."
1 GÚ AN.NA-ak-šu a-ḫu-qar i-lá-qé,and Ahu-waqar will get his 1 talent of tin.
a-na la-ma-sà sí-tim … KIŠIB … mì-x x me-éḫ-ri xx ša ta-áš-pu-ri-ni [...],"To Lamassutum, seal of..., the duplicates which you sent."
a-dí-da ú a-lá-ḫu-um a-šùr-iš-ta-ki-il₅ iš-ú-lu-ma,Adida and Ali-ahum questioned Aššuriš-takil as follows:
3.33333 ma-na KÙ.GI ša-lim-a-šùr a-na na-ru-qí-kà a-dí-im-ma,"Šalim-Aššur invested 3.33333 minas of gold in your joint-stock capital,"
ša 10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR na-ru-qá-kà ú-la-pí-tám,and he wrote an amount of 10 minas of silver for your joint-stock capital.
ša-lim-a-šùr i-na a-lim(ki) a-na li-mì-im ḫa-bu-ul-ma,"Šalim-Aššur is indebted to the eponym in the City,"
ṭup-pá-am ša ší-ip-kà-tim ša-lim-a-šùr ad-ma-ku-ni ṭup-pá-am šu-wa-tí qá-tí li-mì-im ú-kà-al-ma,"and the tablet of the investment Šalim-Aššur made to you, that very tablet is in the eponym's possession,"
KÙ.BABBAR ú né-ma-al-šu dí-in-ma a-ṣé-er li-mì-im li-li-ik-ma,"so pay the silver and the accrued profit, let it go to the eponym,"
ú ṭup-pá-am ša ší-ip-kà-tí-kà a-na ša ki-ma ku-wa-tí li-dí-nu,and then he can give the tablet concerning your capital to your representatives.
iš-tù x 3 ša-na-tim iš-tù bu-ru-uš-ḫa-dim lu ta-li-kam,Three years ago you came from Burušhaddum
ú a-na iš-té-en ú ší-na tap-pá-e-a KÙ.BABBAR ú né-ma-al-šu ta-dí-in,and you have given the silver and the accrued profit to one or two of my partners.
a-na-ku ú ša qá-ta-at a-bi-a-a na-al-pu-tù ni-ta-na-lá-kà-ku-um KÙ.BABBAR ú né-ma-al-šu ta-dá-na-am ú-lá ta-mu-a,"But I and those who signed as my father's guarantors come to you time and again, but you refuse to give the silver and its accrued profit."
a-ṣé-er ki-a-am-ma KÙ.BABBAR 1 ma-na ú 2 ma-na tù-uš-ta-ag-me-er-šu,On top of this you have caused him to have expenses of one or two minas.
KÙ.BABBAR ša li-mì-im a-na ṣí-ib-tim lá i-ma-id-ma,The interest on the silver of the eponym must not increase
É a-bi-a ú ší-ip-kà-tim ša a-bi ad-ma-ku-ni lá i-ta-ba-lá,and my father's house and the investments my father made for you must not be lost.
ší-ma-at KÙ.BABBAR dí-na-ma a-na É li-mì-im,"Give me the agreed amount in silver, let me send it to the eponym's office."
a-na iš-ma-a-šùr DUMU ḫi-na-a a-ta-a-a DUMU bu-ṣí-a ú en-nam-a-šùr DUMU e-lá-ma DUB a-ku-ú-a DUMU a-šùr-i-dí,"To Išme-Aššur, son of hinnāya, Ataya, son of Buṣiya, and Ennam-Aššur, son of Elamma, tablet of Akūa, son of Aššur-idī."
um-ma kà-ru-um a-na ú-bar-tim ša ku-bu-ur-na-at qí-bi-ma,From the Kanesh colony to the trading station Kuburnat say:
a-na-kam me-er-ú ša-lim-a-šùr im-ḫu-ru-ni-a-tí-ma um-ma šu-nu-ma,Here the sons of Šalim-Aššur confronted us and said:
a-šùr-iš-tí-kál DUMU a-šur-SIPA KÙ.BABBAR a-na a-bi-ni ḫa-bu-ul,"Aššuriš-tikal son of Aššur-rē'ī owes silver to our father,"
ú a-we-lam e-mu-qí-in e-ta-ú,and he has spoken harshly to the man.
ma-ṣa-ni a-na ša-sú-ḫi-šu,We take responsibility for his forced transfer.
a-ma-kam a-we-lam iš-tí šé-ep-IŠTAR ší-ip-ri-ni li-sú-ḫa-am,"Extradite the man there together with Šēp-Ištar, our messenger,"
ú a-tù-nu lu e-mu-uq ší-ip-ri-ni,and you must be the executive arm for our messenger.
a-na lu-zi-na DUMU a-šùr-ba-ni a-dí-da DUMU wa-ar-dí-i-li-šu ú a-lá-ḫi-im DUMU šál-ma-a-šùr KIŠIB en-na-su-in DUMU i-d-a-bi-im,"To Luzina son of Aššur-bāni, Adida son of Warad-ilišu and Ali-ahum son of Šalim-Aššur; seal of Enna-Suen son of Iddin-abum."
um-ma ma-ma-ḫi-ir šu-ku-tum ú i-ku-pì-a-ma a-na a-la-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma,"From Man-mahir, Šukkutum and Ikũn-pĩya to Ali-ahum:"
i-na 24 pí-ri-kà-ni ša ḫa-nu ub-lá-ni iš-té-en ḫa-nu a-na li-tab-ší-šu il₅-qé,"Of the 24 textiles that hanu brought, hanu has taken one for his clothes"
iš-té-en a-na ú-ku-ul-tí-šu šu-ut-ma il₅-qé,and he has also taken one to pay for his food.
ší-tí ṣú-ba-tí-kà 22 TÚG 4.83334 GÍN.TA ta-ad-nu,"The rest of your textiles, 22 pieces, were sold for 4.83334 shekels each."
