KIŠIB šu-ku-bi-im DUMU a-šùr-i-dí KIŠIB i-dí-IŠTAR DUMU a-šùr-i-dí sū-in-na-da DUMU en-um-a-šùr tap-pá-i-ni,"Sealed by Šu-Kūbum son of Aššur-idī, by Iddin-Ištar son of Aššur-idī; Suen-nādā son of Ennam-Aššur was our partner."
a-na a-wa-tim a-ni-a-tim kà-ru-um kà-ni-iš ṣa-he-er GAL i-dí-ni-a-tí-ma,The plenary assembly of the Kanesh colony gave us for these proceedings.
ší-bu-tí-ni IGI GÍR ša a-šùr ni-dí-in,And we gave our testimony before Aššur's dagger.
1 TÚG KI ša-ha-ma,1 textile owed by Šahama.
1 TÚG KI sú-is-ha-ra šu wa-áb-ri-ni,"1 textile owed by Su-Ishara, our guest."
IGI a-šùr-ba-ni,Before Aššur-bāni.
a-na ku-zi-zi-a IŠTAR-lá-ma-sí na-áb-sú-in a-na-na a-mur-IŠTAR ša-lim-ar-dí ma-nu-ki-DINGIR-a qí-bi-ma um-ma en-um-a-šur-ma,"To Kuziziya, Ištar-lamassī, Nāb-Suen, Anna-anna, Amur-Ištar, Šalim-wardī and Mannum-kī-iliya from Ennam-Aššur:"
1.5 ma-na 5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu-ki ša ku-ku-wa ù ku-nu-ki-a ù 7 ANŠE.HI.A ṣa-lá-mì ú ú-nu-sú-nu mì-ma a-nim i-a-um ma-nu-ki-ì-lí-a na-áš-a-ku-nu-tí,"1 ½ mina 5 shekels of silver sealed by Kukuwa and by me plus 7 black donkeys with their harness - all this belonging to me, Mannum-kī-iliya brings to you."
a-ṣé-er KÙ.BABBAR a-nim ša ma-nu-ki-ì-lí-a na-áš-a-ku-nu-tí-ni a-na 3 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ú ṣí-ba-tí-šu ša ku-ku-wa a-na ma-nu-ki-a-šur DUMU MAN.IŠTAR ha-bu-lu-ni-ma 20 GÚ SÍG.HI.A a-na ša-pá-ar-tim ú-kà-lu-ni a-na ša ki-ma i-a-tí qí-bi-ma,"In addition to this silver that Mannum-kī-iliya brings to you, for the 3 minas silver and its interest that Kukuwa owes to Mannum-kī-Aššur son of Puzur-Ištar, and for which he holds 20 talents of wool as security - say to my representatives:"
a-ma-kam ma-lá KÙ.BABBAR IŠTAR-lá-ma-sí ù ma-nu-ki-ì-lí-a i-ha-šu-hu-ni KÙ.BABBAR lu i-na ša ba-áb-tí-a ta-am-hu-ra-ni lu KÙ.BABBAR ša a-na ṣé-er a-na-na ku-nu-ki-a ú-šé-bi₄-lá-ni a-na ṣí-ib-tim KÙ.BABBAR ki-ma a-wa-at kà-ri-im dí-na-šu-nu-tí-ma,"Whatever silver Ištar-lamassī and Mannum-kī-iliya ask for there, lend them silver against interest according to the rate of the colony - from what silver you have received from my outstanding claims, or silver I sent to Anna-anna under my seal."
ṭup-pá-am ša IŠTAR-lá-ma-sí ù ma-nu-ki-ì-lí-a me-er-i-ša ša qá-qá-ad šál-mì-šu-nu lu-up-ta-ma a-na am-tí-a ṭup-pá-am dí-na-ma a-dí a-lá-kà-ni,"Then write a tablet for Ištar-lamassī and Mannum-kī-iliya, her son, with joint liability, and give the tablet to my maid so it may remain in her possession until I come."
a-na ṣé-er a-šùr-UTU i-na ba-áb ha-ra-ni-šu né-ru-ub-ma um-ma en-na-sú-in a-na a-šùr-UTU-ma,We entered with Aššur-šamšī when he was about to go on a journey and Ennam-Suen said to Aššur-šamšī:
a-pu-na lá-ma kà-sà-am ni-iš-tí-ú a-wa-tí-im lá-ta-wu-kum li-ba-tim lá ta-ma-lá,"Please, before we drink from the cup I want to declare something to you, do not get angry!"
i-nu-mì i-na wa-áš-ha-ni-a ú-kà-i-lu-ni-ni 2-ma-na KÙ.BABBAR a-ha-ti tù-šé-bi-lá-kà,When they detained me in Wašhaniya did my sister send you to me with 2 minas of silver?
um-ma a-šùr-UTU ke-na tù-šé-bi-lá-ni-ma ú-lá a-dí-na-kum,"Aššur-šamšī answered: ""Sure, she sent me, but I did not give it to you."""
um-ma en-na-sú-in-ma u₄-ma-am a-ha-tí ta-tù-ra-am,"Ennam-Suen then said: ""Today my sister has come back here."""
um-ma ší-it-ma ta-al-tám-nam KÙ.BABBAR ù ṣí-ba-tí ša iš-tù 8 ša-na-tim šé-ṣí-ma dí-nam,And she said: 'You have done me wrong! Produce the silver and its interest due since eight years and give it to me!'
um-ma a-šùr-UTU-ma e-ni-ma-ma a-na šé-ep a-šur-i-mì-tí am-qú-ut,"Aššur-šamšī answered: ""I threw myself down at the feet of Aššur-imittī."""
a-hu-ú-a a-tù-nu a-ma KÙ.GI 15 GÍN ù 1 ma-na sà-am-tum ma-lá ta-le-a-ni É.GAL-lam ṭá-i-ba,"Saying: 'Please, my brothers, here are gold, 15 shekels, and 1 mina of carnelian, appease the palace as well as you can'."
um-ma a-šùr-UTU-ma a-na en-na-sú-in-ma šu-ma KÙ.BABBAR a-na ma-dí-im i-tù-ar al-kam-ma ší-bé-kà la-aṣ-ba-at-ma ma-lá e-pá-ší-im ep-ša-ni,"Aššur-šamšī also said to Ennam-Suen: ""If the silver due has increased much then come here, let me seize your witnesses and do with me what you think best!"""
um-ma en-na-sú-in-ma a-na a-šùr-UTU-ma É.GAL-lúm KÙ.BABBAR ma-dam i-ṣé-ri-a i-šu,"Ennam-Suen answered Aššur-šamšī as follows: ""The palace has a substantial silver claim on me."""
a-na en-nam-a-šur ù a-lá-hi-im qí-bi₄-ma um-ma SIG₅-pí-a-šùr-ma,To Ennam-Aššur and Ali-ahum from Damiq-pī-Aššur:
0.5 ma-na LÁ 1 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ù sà-hi-ir-tám ku-nu-ki-kà na-ki-ru-um ub-lam,They brought me 29 shekels of silver and small goods under seal.
10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR a-ni-na ú e-ni-iš-ta-ru-um ub-lá-ku-nu-tí,Annima and Eništārum brought you 10 minas of silver.
KÙ.BABBAR ša tù-šé-bi-lá-ni a-na ni-ip-lá-tí-a áš-ta-qal,The silver you sent me I have paid to cover my balance payments.
u₄-mu-ú er-ša-sú-ma ILLAT kà-al-a-at,The weather is bad and the caravan has been stopped.
a-hu-a a-tù-nu i-na lu-qú-tim ša tám-kà-ri-im ṣú-ba-tù an-hu-tù-um i-ba-ší-ú,"My dear brothers, among the goods of the merchant there are some old textiles."
ih-da-ma mì-li-ik lu-qú-tí-im mì-il₅-kà,Take care and decide about the goods.
a-hu-a a-tù-nu KÙ.BABBAR ší-im AN.NA x šé-bi-lá-ni-ma,"My dear brothers, send me silver, the proceeds from the tin."
KÙ.BABBAR-pì x i-na ṣé-ri-a šu-uk-na,And deposit my silver to my debit.
a-dí tí-ir-ta-ak-nu i-lá-kà-ni ri-iš lu-qú-tim ú-kà-al,I hold on to the goods until your orders arrive.
a-na e-lá-ma qí-bi₄-ma um-ma a-šùr-ma-lik-ma,"Say to Elamma, thus Aššur-mālik:"
KÙ.BABBAR ša tù-šé-bi₄-lá-ni ù ṭup-pè-kà a-na ma-lá té-er-tí-kà a-na a-lim(ki) uš-té-bi₄-il₅,The silver you sent me and your tablets I have now sent to the City following your instruction.
a-šu-mì KÙ.BABBAR ša É kà-ri-im ša a-na lá-qé-pí-im tù-šé-bi₄-lu KÙ.BABBAR a-na lá-li-im a-dí-in,"As for the silver of the colonial office that you sent for Lā-qēpum, I gave that silver to Lalum."
a-ṣé-er KÙ.BABBAR ù 5 TÚG ša a-di-ú-ma i-na KÙ.BABBAR-áp lá-qé-pí-im-ma i-ší-qí-il₅,"In addition to that silver and the 5 textiles that I deposited, silver has been paid from Lā-qēpum's silver."
