um-ma šu-ku-tum-ma a-na IŠTAR-lá-ma-sí ù ni-ta-ḫšušar qí-bi₄-ma,Thus says Šukkutum to Ištar-lamassī and Nitahšušar: say:
mì-šu ša ta-áš-pu-ra-ni-ni um-ma a-tí-na-ma É-tum a-na lá be-tim i-tù-ar,"Why is it that you have written to me, saying: ""The house is no longer a house""?"
a-pu-tum a-na en-um-a-šùr i-xx-ni-ma e ší-na ga x ša lá ta-ḫa-dì-ri,"Urgent, to Ennam-Aššur ... do not fear!"
a-na IŠTAR-lá-ma-sí qí-bi₄-ma šu-ma a-ḫa-tí a-ta li-ba-am dí-ni-ší-im,"To Ištar-lamassī: ""If you are truly my sister, then encourage her."""
lá ta-ḫa-da-ar,"""Do not fear."""
a-na ni-ta-ḫšušar qí-bi₄-ma TÚG-pì-ri-kà-ni ša e-zi-bu na-pí-ší-šu-nu,"To Nitahšušar: ""Air the pirikannu-textiles that I left."""
ù ṭup-pu-ú lu ša-ṣú-ru,"""Also, the tablets should be guarded."""
pì-ri-kà-nu ša ma-tí ù tí-bu-lá ma-a-x iš-ta-ú-mu-ni a-dí en-um-a-šùr i-lá-kà-ni a ma-ma-an lá tù-šé-ri,"""Do not release the pirikannu-textiles which Mati? and Tibula have bought to anyone before Ennam-Aššur arrives."""
x GÍN KÙ.BABBAR (d)UTU-tap-pá-i ub-lá-ki-im,Šamaš-tappā’ī brought you x shekels of silver.
1 GÍN KÙ.GI ù x GÍN KÙ.BABBAR i-ku-pì-a ub-lá-ki-im,Ikūn-pīya brought you 1 shekel of gold and x shekels of silver.
um-ma šu-ta-mu-zi e-lá-a en-um-a-šùr ù lá-ma-sí-ma a-na en-um-a-šùr ù a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi₄-ma,"Thus say Šu-Tammuzī, Elaya, Ennam-Aššur and Lamassī to Ennam-Aššur and Ali-ahum:"
a-ma-la na-áš-pé-er-tí-ku-nu ra-bi-ṣa-am ni-ḫu-za-ku-nu-tí,"In accordance with your missive, we have hired an attorney for you."
a-bi-a DUMU be-e-be ra-bi₄-iṣ-ni,"Abiya, son of Bebe, is our attorney."
i-na ša-am-ší ša ra-bi-ṣú-um e-ra-ba-ni iḫ-da-ma i-zi-za-ma,Take care to stand by the very day the attorney arrives.
lu DAM.GÀR a-bi-ku-nu lu ša a-wa-tám tí-šu-a-ni ra-bi-ṣú-um i-na ša-ḫa-tí-ku-nu li-zi-iz-ma,Let the attorney assist you with regard to your father's agents and those with whom you have a dispute.
i-na KÙ.BABBAR pá-ni-ma a-šar ta-ma-ḫa-ra-ni KÙ.BABBAR ša É a-lim(ki) šu-ta-aṣ-bi-ta-ma,"Of the first silver, wherever you receive it, collect the silver of the City Hall."
ma-lá a-bu-ku-nu ḫa-bu-lu KÙ.BABBAR ku-un-kà-ma šé-bi-lá-nim,"As much as your father owes, seal the silver and send it."
ra-bi₄-ṣú-um iš-tí-ku-nu li-ik-nu-uk-ma KÙ.BABBAR šé-bi-lá-nim-ma li-ma-am lu nu-ša-bi,"The attorney should seal it with you, and then send the silver so we can satisfy the eponym."
ṣí-ba-at ṣí-ib-tim lá i-ma-i-da-ku-nu-tí-ma li-ba-ku-nu e im-ra-aṣ,The compound interest should not grow too big for you and make you unhappy.
ma-lá e-ṭá-ar É a-bí₄-ku-nu ep-ša,Act so as to save your father's house.
šu-ma ta-da-ga-lá-ma ṭup-pu ḫa-ru-mu-tum ú ba-ba-a-tum ru-qá-tum i-ba-ší-ú ṭup-pí ku-un-kà-ma a-na DUMU um-me-a-nim ke-nim ša ki-ma ku-nu-tí pí-iq-da-ma,"If you observe that there are certified deeds and credits outstanding on long terms, then seal the tablets and entrust them to a trustworthy affiliated trader like yourselves."
u₄-me-e-ku-nu ba-lu-um mì-ma-ma lá tù-ri-qá-ma lá ta-sà-ḫu-ra,Do not let your time pass for no reason and do not delay.
iš-tí ra,with the attorney.
KIŠIB a-lá-ḫi-im KIŠIB a-li-li KIŠIB a-bí₄-lá KIŠIB lá-qé-ep,"Seal of Ali-ahum, seal of Ali-ilī, seal of Abila, seal of Lā-qēp."
ša i-na ba-áb-tim ša a-šùr-be-el-ma-al-ki-im ša iš-ti DUMU a-tù-ri-a ù a-mur-a-šùr ḫi-na-a iṣ-bu-tù-ma a-na e-lá-ma ip-qí-du,What Hinnaya had seized as part of the outstanding claims of Aššur-bēl-malkim from the son of Aturiya and Amur-Aššur and had entrusted to Elamma.
2 ma-na 13.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am e-lá-ma a-na a-lá-ḫi-im ù a-li-li ip-qí-du,"2 minas 13.5 shekels of refined silver, which Elamma in turn had entrusted to Ali-ahum and Ali-ilī."
KÙ.BABBAR a-na a-lá-ḫi-im a-li-li ù ḫi-na-a a ba-re-šu-nu i-lá-ak,"This silver will become the joint responsibility of Ali-ahum, Ali-ilī, and Hinnaya."
a-na É šál-ma-a-šùr a-na a-wa-tim né-ru-ub-ma,We entered Šalim-Aššur's house for the legal proceedings.
um-ma šál-ma-a-šùr-ma i-a-tí a-na bu-ru-uš-ḫa-dim i-na ma-ak-sú-e-im a-na ḫu-bu-ul ÌR a-bu-ša-lim ša-qá-lim i-ra-de₈-ú-ni,"Šalim-Aššur said: ""While they are leading me to Burušhaddum in fetters to pay the debt of the slave Abu-šalim."""
a-ta 30 (TÚG)ku-ta-ni ù ANŠE ṣa-lá-ma-am ša ÌR ta-lá-qé-e,"""Will you take 30 textiles and a black donkey from the slave?"""
ša-lim-a-šur ša ni-iš a-lim(ki) úz-na-tí-ni il₅-pu-ut,Šalim-Aššur informed us about what had been sworn by the City.
um-ma ša-lim-a-šur-ma a-šar ÌR a-na ÌR-dí-kà lá i-tù-ru-ú ma-a a-na ÌR-dí-a i-tù-wa-ar,"Šalim-Aššur said: ""Since the slave does not claim against your slave, will he then claim against my slave?"""
um-ma šu-be-lúm-ma šu-ma a-na ku-a-im i-tù-a-ar a-na TÚG.ḪI.A ù ANŠE.ḪI.A a-za-za-kum,"Šu-Bēlum answered: ""If he claims against yours, then I guarantee the textiles and the donkey for you."""
a-na a-wa-tim a-ni-a-tim kà-ru-um kà-ni-iš i-dí-ni-a-tí-ma IGI GÍR ša a-šùr ší-bu-tí-ni ni-dí-in,"The Kanesh colony gave us a verdict for these proceedings, and we gave our testimony before Aššur's dagger."
IGI ú-ra-a IGI ì-lí-dan IGI ma-ni-um-ba-lúm-a-šùr,"Witnessed by Uraya, by Ilī-dan, by Mannum-balum-Aššur."
ṭup-pu-um ša 10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša PÚZUR-a-šur ù PÚZUR-(d)IŠKUR,A tablet about 10 minas of silver of Puzur-Aššur and Puzur-Adad.
ṭup-pu-um ša 4 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša PÚZUR-a-šur,A tablet about 4 minas of silver of Puzur-Aššur.
ṭup-pu-um ša 10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša a-sà-nim,A tablet about 10 minas of silver of Asānum.
ṭup-pu-um ša 10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša al-pì-lí,A tablet about 10 minas of silver of Alpī-ilī.
ṭup-pu-um ša 10 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša a-sà-nim ú PÚZUR-a-šur,A tablet about 10 minas of silver of Asānum and Puzur-Aššur.
ṭup-pu-um ša 5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša a-šùr-ṣú-lu-li,A tablet about 5 minas of silver of Aššur-ṣulūlī.
ṭup-pu-um ša 17 ma-na 15 GÌN ša e-na-na-tim,A tablet about 17 minas 15 shekels of silver of Ennanātum.
ṭup-pu-um ša ḫu-bu-ul a-bí-ni i-na ku-bu-ur-na-at al-qé-šu,A tablet about a debt of our father; I obtained it in Kuburnat.
17 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ší-im e-ma-ri-im,"17 shekels of silver, the price of a donkey."
30 ma-na URUDU IŠTAR-pí-lá-aḫ,30 minas of copper of Ištar-pilah.
a-na ar-be-e-šu x ú-kà-pu-ú ša-pì-ú-tim,Four thick saddlecloths.
9 ma-na URUDU SIG₅ i ší-im sú-ub-ri-im,9 minas of refined copper from the price of a slave.
1 ma-na URUDU ší-kam iš-tí DUMU IŠTAR-ba-ni,1 mina of šikkum-copper with the son of Ištar-bani.
2 kà-ar-pát kà-mu-nu,2 jars of cumin.
mì-ma a-nim i-na du-ur-ḫu-mì-it i-ba-ší,All this is available in Durhumit.
10 pí-ri-kà-nu 1 GÚ SÍG.ḪI.A 2 ú-kà-pé-e,"10 pirikannu-textiles, 1 talent of wool, 2 saddle-rugs."
80 lu-ur-ma-tum 10 ma-na ì.GIŠ sà-ar-dam,"80 pomegranates, 10 minas of sardum oil."
sà-áp-tí-nam ni-ib-ra-ra-am 2 ší-it-re-e ša za-al-pá,"A saptinnu-textile, a nibraru-textile, 2 scarfs from Zalpa."
2 e-ma-re ú ú-nu-sú-nu,2 donkeys with their harness.
mì-ma a-nim a-na a-šùr-i-mì-tí a-dín,All this I gave to Aššur-imitti.
[...] ù i-na ma-lá i-na … ba-ab-tí-a KÙ.BABBAR ta-ma-ḫa-ra-ni …,... and from what you receive from my outstanding claims ...
en-um-a-šùr ṭù-ur-da-nim …,... send Ennam-Aššur ...
iš-tí-in i-na ra-dí-i a-… i-na kà-ṣa-ri-a ša ta-na-ta …-lá … ki-il₅-a-ma i-re-ší-ku-nu li-zi-iz-ma ba-ab-tí ša-áš-qí-lá,"One of the guides ... of my harnessors that you observe, keep him and let him serve you, and have my outstanding claims paid."
a-ḫu-ú-a a-tù-nu iḫ-da-ma … ba-ab-tí-a ša kà-ni-iš-ki KÙ.BABBAR 10 ma-na ša-áš-qí-lá-ma gi-im-lá-ni,"My dear brothers, take care to have paid at least 10 minas of my outstanding claims in Kanesh and do me a favour."
i-na a-al ší-a-ma-tim wa-áš-ba-ku,I am staying in a city where purchases can be made.
a-šu-mì ša en-um-be-lim šu-ma um-me-a-nu-um ša ki-ma qá-qí-dí-ku-nu e-pá-al-ku-nu a ma-lá ṭup-pì-šu AN.NA ù TÚG.ḪI.A dí-na-ma ṭup-pá-am lu-up-ta,"As to the matter of Ennam-Bēlum, if an investor as safe as you yourselves will take responsibility for you, then sell the tin and textiles in accordance with his tablet and write a tablet."
šu-ma um-me-a-nu-um lá e-pá-al-ku-nu 15.5 ma-na 3 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR le-qé-a,"If an investor does not answer you, then take 15.5 minas 3 shekels of silver."
ù šu-ma lá ki-a-am x ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ki-il₅-a-ma a-dí e-lá-i-a ma-ma-an … a-li … a-na [...] …-na-nim li-il₅ me lá ni,"But, if it not so, then hold on to x minas of silver and noone must ... until I come up. ..."
a-na be-lu-ba-ni ù a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma um-ma zu-ku-a-ma,To Bēlum-bāni and Ali-ahum from Zukuwa:
2 le-ú e-lá-nu-ma ù 2 ri-ik-sí AN.NA ku-nu-ki-a x ŠU.NÍGIN 35 ma-na AN.NA ša a-šur-ba-ni DUMU i-dí-a-bi₄-im na-áš-ú-ni,"2 extra ingots and 2 bundles of tin under my seal, in all 35 minas of tin, that Aššur-bāni son of Iddin-abum brings;"
2 ri-ik-sí ku-nu-ki-a ŠU.NÍGIN 33 ma-na AN.NA ša a-mur-a-šùr DUMU a-šùr-DU₁₀ na-áš-ú,"2 bundles under my seal, in all 33 minas of tin, that Amur-Aššur son of Aššur-ṭāb brings;"
ŠU.NÍGIN 1 GÚ 8 ma-na AN.NA ša ik-ri-be a-mur-a-šùr …-GAL ga … na-áš-ú,"in all 1 talent 8 minas of tin from the votive offerings Amur-Aššur, ...-rabi and ... bring."
… a-ḫu-ú-a a-tù-nu iḫ-da-ma i-na (d)UTU-ši e-ru-bu-ni-ni AN.NA pu-uṭ-ra-ma sà-ni-qá-ma sí-ni-iq-tí AN.NA-ki-a,"My dear brothers, take care to unpack the tin the very day it arrives, check it and send me word about the check of my tin"
tí-ir-ta-ak-nu li-li-kam-ma li-bi₄ lá ip-ta-na-ri-id,so I shall not worry all the time.
12.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ig-ri-šu-nu dí-na-šu-nu-tí,"Give them their wages, 12.5 shekels of silver."
an-ni-ki É-be-et iš-té-en-x i-na ba-ri-ku-nu li-ib-ší,Let my tin stay in one of your houses.
a-lá-ḫa-am ú ṣú-ḫa-ri ma-lá wa-áš-bu-ni ù e-ma-ri ša ili₅-we-da-ku ú-šé-ri-a-ni ù i-a-am ša wa-ší-ib-ru-ba-ni ir-dí-a-ku-nu-tí-ni ù ú-nu-sú a-lá-ḫu-um li-ir-dí-a-am,"As for Ali-ahum and the servants who are present - plus the donkeys that Ilī-wēdāku conducted to me plus my own that Wašibru-bāni led to you, including its harness - let Ali-ahum lead that to me."
[...] … ṭup-pá-am ni-mar,... we shall see the tablet ...
… x-in KÙ.BABBAR,... silver ...
… ša-áp-ra-tù-šu,... his pledges ...
… ub-lá-ki-im,... he brought to you (fem.) ...
… x-lá-ni-ší-na … ú-kà-lu-nim [...],... they hold ...
KIŠIB ša-lim-a-šur a-na en-nam-a-šur ù a-lá-ḫi-im,Sealed by Šalim Aššur; to Ennam-Aššur and Ali-ahum.
ša-na-am ša 20 ma-na ma-… [...],A kettle of 20 minas ...
um-ma bé-lá-num ù ḫi-na-a-ma a-na e-lá-ma qí-bi-ma,"Thus Bēlānum and hinnāya, say to Elamma:"
wa-ar-ki-kà-ma 11 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ù 16 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša a-šu-mì KÙ.GI en-nam-a-šùr tù-ša-ḫi-zu me-ra-kà a-na en-nam-a-šur ú-šé-bi-lam,"After you had left your son sent 11 minas of silver and the 16 minas of silver, on which you had given Ennam-Aššur instructions concerning gold, to Ennam-Aššur."
16 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR en-nam-a-šur il₅-qé-ma 2 ma-na KÙ.GI ù 11 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR a-ṣé-ri-ni ú-šé-bi-lam,Ennam-Aššur took these 16 minas of silver and sent 2 minas of gold and the 11 minas of silver to us.
wa-ar-kà-tám 18 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR DUMU ṣa-lá-mì-im ú-šé-ṣí-am,Later the son of Ṣallāmum produced 18 minas of silver.
KÙ.BABBAR ù KÙ.GI pá-ni-am ú-ša-ší-ib TUR GAL nu-pá-ḫe-er-ma a-ṣé-er ša ki-ma ku-a-tí a-na kà-ni-iš nu-uš-té-ri-ib,This silver and the earlier amount of gold he ... We collected everything and brought (it) into Kanesh to your representatives (saying):
i té-er-tí-ni pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR KÙ.GI a-na DUMU ṣa-lá-mì-im pí-iq-da-ma a-ṣé-er e-lá-ma lu-bi-il₅,'At the instruction of Pilah-Ištar you must entrust the gold to the son of Ṣallāmum to bring it to Elamma'.
4 GÚ 42 ma-na URUDU iš-tí i-dí-(d)MAR.TU,4 talents 42 minas of copper with Iddin-Aurum.
0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR bé-ú-lá-at ki-ta-a,"0.5 mina of silver, working capital of Kitaya."
8 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR KI šu-li DUMU PUZUR₄-a-be-eḫ,"8 minas of silver with Šuli, son of Puzur-Abeh."
4 ma-na 3.83334 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR KI id-na-a,"4 minas 3.83333 shekels of silver with Idnāya,"
ITU.KAM ma-ḫu-ur-ì-lí li-mu-um šu-da-a 1.25 GÍN.TA ṣí-ib-tám ú-ṣa-áb,"month IV, eponymy of Šudāya; he will add 1 1 / 4 shekel per (mina per month) as interest."
1 GÚ 20 ma-na URUDU ù 0.33333 ma-na 5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR KI i-ba-a,1 talent 20 minas of copper and 25 shekels <of silver(?)> with Ibaya.
8 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR KI i-ku-mì-šar,8 shekels of silver with Ikūn-Mīšar.
2 ma-na 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR KI a-šùr-du-ri li-mu-um ip-ḫu-ru-um,"2 minas 10 shekels of silver with Aššur-dūrī, year eponymy of Iphurum."
1.5 GÍN.TA ṣí-ib-tám ú-ṣa-áb,He will add 1.5 shekel per (mina per month).
0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR KI ba-al-ṭù-im,0.5 mina of silver with Balṭu'um.
0.33333 ma-na 5 GÍN bé-ú-lá-at gal-da-a,25 shekels (of silver) working capital of Galdaya.
1 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR KI gal-da-a,1 mina of silver with Galdaya.
um-ma ša-lim-a-šùr-ma a-na i-dí-a-bi-im en-na-nim i-na-aḫ-DINGIR ma-ma-ḫi-ir en-um-a-šùr ù a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bí-ma,"From Šalim-Aššur to Iddin-abum, Ennānum, Inah-ilī, Man-mahir, Ennam-Aššur and Ali-ahum:"
x ṭup-pé-e-a ḫa-ru-mu-tim ša ba-a-ba-tí-a am-ra-ma ma-ma-an KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN ḫa-bu-lá-ni KÙ.BABBAR ù ṣí-ba-sú ša-áš-qí-lá,"Check my certified tablets concerning my outstanding claims, and make anyone who owes me a single shekel of silver pay the silver and its interest."
a-šar ta-na-ṭá-lá-ni a-tù-nu-ma a-ma-kam mì-il₅-kà iḫ-da-ma KÙ.BABBAR ša-áš-qí-lá-ma i-na pá-nim-ma šé-bí-lá-nim,You yourselves must decide there in whatever matter you observe. Take care to have the silver paid and send it to me as soon as possible.
KÙ.BABBAR ša ba-a-ba-tí-a lu ša-li-iṭ a-li-bi lu-qú-tí-a lá ta-sà-ḫi-a,The silver from my outstanding claims must be available; do not make trouble (mixing it) with my merchandise.
7.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR qá-tí ša tù-um-li-a-i-im,"7 ½ minas of silver, the share of the man from Tumliya;"
2 ma-na.TA KÙ.BABBAR ù 80 80 ú-ṭù-tù-um mì-iš-lu-um GIG ṣí-ib-tám iš-tù MU.4.ŠÈ tal-qé-a,"you received interest for 4 years at 2 minas of silver each and two times 80 (sacks) of grain, half of it wheat."
8 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ù 3 me-at 20 na-ru-uq ú-ṭù-tù-um ší-im ú-ṭí-tí-a ù KÙ.BABBAR ṣí-ib-tí šu-ul-ṭá-ma šé-bi₄-lá-nim,8 minas of silver plus 320 sacks of grain – make the proceeds from my grain and my interest on the silver available and send it.
ù šu-ma ta-áš-bi-tí qá-tí i-du-nu-ni-ku-nu-tí le-qé-a,"And if they will give you the full payment on my share, then take it."
ù šu-ma ma-ma-an i-na tap-pá-i-a lá ma-gi₅-ir-ku-nu qá-tí dí-na iš-té-ni-iš KÙ.BABBAR šé-bí-lá-nim,"Also, if any of my partners do not agree with you, then sell the share. Send me all of the silver."
1 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ù 40 na-ru-uq ú-ṭù-tù-um ṣí-i,"1 mina of silver and 40 sacks of grain, the interest."
a-na lu-zi-na a-dí-da ù a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi₄-ma um-ma en-na-sú-in-ma,"To Luzina, Adida and Ali-ahum; from Enna-Suen:"
5.33333 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am PUZUR₄-a-šùr DUMU a-zu-za ḫa-bu-lam,Puzur-Aššur son of Azuza owes me 5.3333 minas of refined silver.
iš-tù ITU.KAM na-ar-ma-ak-a-šùr li-mu-um en-na-sú-in a-na 7 ITU.KAM i-ša-qal,He is to pay within 7 months from the month Narmak-Aššur in the eponymy of Enna-Suen.
šu-ma lá iš-qú-ul ki-ma a-wa-at kà-ri-im ṣí-ib-tám ú-ṣa-áb,"If he has not paid (in time), he is to add interest in accordance with the rule of the colony."
a-ḫu-ú-a be-lu-ú-a a-tù-nu a-wi-lúm a-dí ma-lá ù ší-ni-šu iṣ-li-a-ni,"My dear brothers and lords, the man has cheated me once or twice."
ṣa-áb-ta-šu-ma KÙ.BABBAR ù ṣí-ba-sú ma-lá ta-le-e-a-ni ša-áš-qí-lá-šu-ma AN.NA ša-ma-nim-ma ku-un-kà-ma a-na DUMU um-me-a-nim ke-nim dí-na-ma ku-nu-ki-ku-nu lu-ub-lam,"Seize him and have him pay the silver and as much interest as you can manage and then buy tin for me, seal it and give it to a reliable affiliated trader who can bring it to me under your seals."
