ki-ma ṣú-ba-tí sà-sà-am il₅-pu-tù um-ma a-na-ku-ma,"and since my textiles are infested with moths, I thought:"
iš-tí lu-qú-tí-a le-ru-ub-ma bu-lá-tí-a lu-pá-ḫi-ir-ma ú KÙ.BABBAR 10 ma-na ša qá-ru-bi-im i-ṣé-er tám-kà-ri-a lá-al-qé,"Let me enter with my goods and collect my assets, so that I may receive some 10 minas of silver that may be collected from my customers."
a-na kà-ni-iš i bu-lá-tí-a le-ru-ba-am,Let me enter Kanesh with my assets.
a-ဦu-a a-t္-nu a-dအ ဧa a-za-ku-ဴ a-ma-kam iဧ-tအ ဧa ki-ma me-er-e um-me-a-nim ဧa a-ma-kam wa-အဧ-bu-ni a-we-li i-na a-wa-tim ma-qအ-ta-ma pအ-ဧu-nu li-im-dအ-nim-ma uဵ-me-e ဧa ဧa-kအ-nim li-iဧ-ku-nu-nim-ma a-na kအ-ri-im qအ-ri-ba-ni,"My dear brothers, until I clear myself, you there - together with the representatives of the affiliated traders who are staying there - should pester the men for the case, learn what they have to say and let them set terms, and make me approach the colony."
i-be-sa-e ú ma-na-aḫ-tí šu-nu-ma i-dí-ú ù ba-lu-um um-me-a-ni-a,"They know the losses and the maintenance, but without permission from my investors."
a-wa-tù-šu-nu ša šál-ma-a-šùr šu-bé-lúm ki-ma DAM i-sú-rik₁₃ DUMU.MÍ i-sú-rik₁₃ ù DUMU.MÍ i-dí-a-bi-im ra-bi-ṣum ù šu-be-lúm KI ša-lim-a-šur ni-iš a-lim(ki) it-mu-ú-ma a-wa-tù-šu-nu gám-ra,"Their case concerning Šalim-Aššur - Šu-Bēlum for the wife of Issu-arik, the daughter of Issu-arik and the daughter of Iddin-abum, the attorney and Šu-Bēlum swore an oath on the City with Šalim-Aššur and their case was concluded."
[...] ù a-ḫu-šu i-lu-ku-ni-ma ša-lim-a-šùr a-na lu-qú-tim AN.NA ù TÚG.ḪI.A ša-lim-a-šùr ú-kà-nu-ni,"... and his brother will come and confirm Šalim-Aššur for the goods, the tin and textiles."
a-šùr-ta-ak-lá-ku ra-bi-ṣú-um,Aššur-taklāku was the attorney.
a-na lu-qú-tim a-ni-tim šu-be-lúm a-ša-at i-sú-rik₁₃ DUMU.MÍ i-sú-rik₁₃ ù DUMU.MÍ i-dí-a-bi-im a-na ša-lim-a-šùr šu-ku-bi₄-im ù a-ḫi-šu ú-lá i-tù-ru,"Šu-Bēlum, the wife of Issu-arik, the daughter of Issu-arik and the daughter of Iddin-abum must not raise claim to these goods against Šalim-Aššur, Šu-Kūbum or his brother."
šu-ma i-tù-ru šu-be-lúm ù MAŠKIM ú-bu-bu-šu-nu,"If they do raise claim, Šu-Bēlum and the attorney will clear them."
IGI (d)MAR.TU-ba-ni,"Witnessed by Amurrum-bāni,"
IGI a-šùr-i-dí,"by Aššur-idī,"
IGI šu-ku-bi-im,"by Šu-Kūbum,"
IGI šu-ma-li-ba-a-šùr,by Šumma-libbi-Aššur.
[...] ma i me-er-e-a É-tí ma-ma-an iš-ta-am,"... why, someone from among my sons bought the house."
lá-ma-sí i qé-er-bi₄-im tù-ša-áb,Lamassī lives in it.
šu-ma be-tí DAM.GÀR-ru-um lá i-tí-dí-in i be-tim ša la-ma-… [...],"If the merchant has not given my house, in the house of Lama..."
a-na a-la-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma um-ma a-mur-IŠTAR-ma,To Ali-ahum from Amur-Ištar:
9 GÚ 17 ma-na URUDU qá-tí a-bi-ni a-šur-iš-ta-ki-il₅ É kà-ri-im im-ḫu-ur,"Aššuriš-takil received 9 talents 17 minas of copper, our father's share, in the office of the colony."
a-na-ku ša tù-ša-ḫi-zi-ni um-ma a-ta-ma,"As for me, you gave me instructions, saying:"
URUDU qá-tí a-bi-ni a-na URUDU SIG₅ li-tù-ur-ma i-ṣé-er DUMU um-me-a-nim i-dí-i,the copper from our father's share should be converted to good copper and give it on credit to an affiliated trader.
lá-ma URUDU i-na É kà-ri-im úṣ-a-ni iš xx ma-na a-wa-tum i-x-x-iš-ma,"Before the copper left the office of the colony, ... minas ... a matter,"
10 GÚ URUDU lá-mu-nam qá-tí a-bi₄-ni É a-šur-iš-ta-ki-il₅ i-lá-qé-ma,"and he will receive 10 talents of bad copper, our father's share, in Aššuriš-takil's house,"
ru-bu-a-ú-ma 2 GÚ 30 ma-na URUDU SIG₅ x ṭup-pu-šu al-pu-ut,and at one to four I wrote his tablet for 2 talents 30 minas of good copper.
URUDU SIG₅ x a-na 40 ḫa-am-ša-tim i-ša-qal,He will pay the good copper in 40 weeks.
ù 2 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša bé-lúm-ba-ni i li-bi a-ni-na aṣ-ba-at-ma,"Also, I seized 2 minas of silver belonging to Bēlum-bāni from Annina,"
ù 2 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša aṣ-bu-tù a-ṣé-er ṭup-pí-šu ú-ṭá-ḫi-ma,and then I added the 2 minas of silver that I seized to his tablet
ṭup-pu-šu ša KÙ.BABBAR ù URUDU SIG₅ al-pu-ut,and wrote his tablet concerning the silver and good copper.
KÙ.BABBAR ù URUDU a-na 40 ḫa-am-ša-tim i-ša-qal,He is to pay the silver and the copper in 40 weeks.
i-na 9 GÚ 17 ma-na URUDU URUDU qá-tí a-bi-ni a-šur-iš-ta-ki-il₅ im-ḫu-ru-ú,"Of the 9 talents 17 minas of copper, the copper from our father's share, (that) Aššuriš-takil received,"
ŠÀ.BA 4 GÚ 37 ma-na URUDU lá-mu-nam a-na ma-lá na-am-gu₅-ra-ni-ni a-ni-na il₅-qé,thereof Annina took 4 talents 37 minas of bad copper in accordance with our agreement.
ší-tí URUDU-im um-ta-sí-iḫ lá-qá-am lá,He looked down on the rest of the copper; he will not take it.
x 5 GÍN AN.NA a-na na-áb-ri-tim ša e-ma-ri ù ḫar-lá i-na ra-mì-ni-a áš-qú-ul,x + 5 shekels of tin for the paddock for the donkeys and (for) harla I paid myself.
12 GÍN AN.NA 3 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR 4 ma-na URUDU 70 sí-pá-ra-tim a-na qá-tí šé-ep-IŠTAR ša-li-wa-ar-dí a-dí-in,"I gave 12 shekels of tin, 3 shekels of silver, 4 minas of copper, and 70 shells to the hand of Šēp-Ištar and Šaliwardi."
5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pu-um i-na ší-im SÍG.ḪI.A ša ú-ší-na-lam PUZUR₄-ša-du-we DUMU lá-qé-ep il₅-qé,Puzur-šadu'e son of Lā-qēp has received 5 minas of refined silver from the proceeds of Ušinalam's wool.
IGI a-šùr-GAL DUMU ma-nu-um-šum-šum,"Witnessed by Aššur-rabi son of Mannum-šumšu,"
IGI en-na-sú-in DUMU i-dí-a-bi-im,"by Enna-Suen son of Iddin-abum,"
IGI i-dí-a-šùr bu du ú,by Iddin-Aššur.
a-na ku-li-a ḫa-nu-nu ú-ṣur-ša-a-šur a-šur-lá-ma-sí a-na u-ṣú-ur-ša-a-šur qí-bí-ma,"Say to Kuliya, Hanunu, Usur-sa-Assur, (and) Assur-lamassi, (in particular) to Usur-sa-Assur:"
um-ma pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR,thus Pilah-Istar:
0.33333 ma-na 7 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša a-šur ša ma-ṣa-ar-tí ù be-té-e iš-tù 4 ša-na-té-e a-dí-na-ku,"""27 shekels of silver of Assur, of the strong room and the house(s), I gave you four years ago."
um-ma a-ta-ma a-ḫi-i i-na ma-a-ma a-ma-ḫa-ar-ma KÙ.BABBAR 3 ma-na na-ší ú KÙ.BABBAR-áp-kà ú-šé-ba-lá-ku,"You (then) said: 'I will turn to my brother in Mamma who is carrying 3 minas of silver, and I will send you your silver."
ú KÙ.BABBAR 1 GÍN a ni-na-ša ú-šé-ba-lá-ku,"Moreover, I will send to you, to Nenassa every (possible) shekel of silver'."
ú ma-a iš-tù 4 ša-na-té-e KÙ.BABBAR-áp A-šur ta-ma-kà-ar ú a-dí u₄-mì-im a-nim tù-uk-ta-ṣí-dá-ni,"Now, realize well that since four years you use the silver of Assur for trading purposes and that you have kept me waiting until this very day!"
KÙ.BABBAR ú ḫa-ra-na-tí-šu ṣa-ba-at-ma a-na ša ki-ma i-a-tí dí-in,Get hold of the silver or what has been acquired with it during its journeys and give it to my representative(s).
KÙ.BABBAR e-lá ta-dí-in-ma a-na u₄-mì-im wa-ar-ke-e li-ba-kà i-ma-ra-IṢ,Don't fail to give that silver lest you will regret it afterwards!
a-na a-wa-tí ša ta-at-wu-ú ú a-na-ku a-wa-at ša a-ḫi eb-ri lá-IS-me-e,"As for the words you spoke, I too can listen to the words of colleagues and friends."
ki-ma e-ta-wu-ni ta-ša-x,"You must comply(?) with what I said!""."
a-ma-kam i-na be-el id-ma-tim ša ki-ma um-mì-a-né ma-ma-an mì-ma ú-lá i-ṭá-ḫi,Over there no one of the share-holders representing the investors shall approach anything.
a ma-lá ṭup-pì-im ša a-lim(ki) i-ša-ri-iq-šu-um,"According to the tablet of the City, (if he does) it will be considered as stolen by him."
[...] …-1 TÚG … pí-ri-kà-nu …-5 TÚG …-im ú …-bu …-x TÚG …-ni ša be-lá-nim … …-mu …-nam …-ma a-ṣé-er … ú-bi-il₅ … pí-ri-kà-nu …-lu-tim …-x ú a-ḫa-ma … 2 pí-ri-kà-an ku-nu-ki-a na-ar-bu-tim …-tim mì-ma a-nim a-na a-šur-e-nam [...],"to the address of .......... he brought ......... -textiles ... ... ... ... ... ... ... and separately 2 -textiles with my seals, soft ones? [and ... ... ... ...] ones, all this to / for Aššur-ennam ... ..."
um-ma ša-lim-a-šur a-na en-nam-a-šur ú a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma,From Šalim-Aššur to Ennam-Aššur and Ali-ahum:
KÙ.BABBAR pá-ḫi-ra-ma i-na ku-nu-ki-ku-nu ku-un-kà-ma a-na bé-tí-a a-šar ša-ṣú-ru-ni li-ni-dí,"Collect the silver, seal it with your seals and let it be placed in my house where it can be well guarded."
2 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša qá-tí-ni [...],2 minas of silver from our account ...
10 ma-na … a-šur … a-na … … … … 2.5-GÍN KÙ.BABBAR aḫ-bu-ul-šum IGI ku-ra DUMU na-ra-am-ZU IGI a-šùr-DU₁₀ DUMU lu-lu-ú,"10 minas ... Assur ... to ... ... ... ... 2.5 shekels of silver I lent to him. Before Kura, son of Naram-Suen, before Assur-tab, son of Lulu."
12 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša a-al-DU₁₀ a-na kur-ub-sú-in ḫa-bu-lu-ma en-na-sú-in qá-ta-tù-ni,"12 shekels of silver, which Āl-ṭāb owes to Kurub-Suen and (for which) Ennam-Suen was guarantor,"
KÙ.BABBAR ki-ma kur-ub-sú-in pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR il₅-qé en-na-sú-in ki-ma a-al-DU₁₀ KÙ.BABBAR iš-qú-ul-šum,"Pilah-Ištar collected that silver in the name of Kurub-Suen, Ennam-Suen paid it to him in the name of Āl-ṭāb."
šu-ma kur-ub-sú-in a-na a-al-DU₁₀ i-tù-wa-ar pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR ú-ba-áb-šu,"If Kurub-Suen raises a claim (for it) for against Al-ṭāb, Pilah-Ištar will clear him."
KÙ.BABBAR i-na li-mì-im šu-da-a … ITU.KAM ku-zal-li il₅-qé,"He collected the silver during the eponymy of Šudaya, in the month XI."
IGI (d)IŠKUR.ILLAT IGI ir-am-a-šùr DUMU ì-dí-ba-ni,"Witnessed by Adad-ellat, by Ir'am-Aššur, son of Idi-bāni."
um-ma e-na-aḫ-DINGIR-ma a-na a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma,From Enah-ilī to Ali-ahum:
a-pu-tum i-na ša-am-ší ṭup-pá-am ta-ša-me-ú tí-ib-a-ma a-tal-kam,Urgent! The very day you hear the letter you must set out and come.
a-na ša-lim-a-šùr a-bi-ku-nu iš-tí xx-tim [...] xx … i-ba-ší-ú,To your (plur.) father Šalim-Aššur ... what is present ...
… URUDU SIG₅ ša qá-sú iš-… a-na ni-bi-it URUDU SIG₅ IGI ší-bi ta-aḫ-sí-is-ta-kà i-dí-ma,"copper of good quality that he has personally ... deposit a memorandum before witnesses with specifications of the good copper,"
tí-ib-a-ma a-tal-kam,and set out and come here.
ú a-na-kam iš-tí um-me-a-ni lu-za-ki-ku-nu,"Also, I shall clear you here with the investors."
i-na ba-ri-ku-nu lá tù-uš-té-ṣa-a-ma um-me-a-nu lá kà-…,"You must not quarrel with each other ..., and the investors should not ..."
a-we-lá-tù-ku-nu … lá i-ḫa-li-qá … ta-ša-lá-ta …,your women ...should not be lost ... you (plur.) must (not) act rashly ...
KIŠIB en-nam-a-šur DUMU um-ma-sá,"Seal of Ennam-Aššur, son of Ummassa."
a-šur-DÙL DUMU a-šùr-šadí-li ki-ma ku-li-a DUMU a-lá-bi₄-im a-na a-šur-e-mu-qí DUMU šu-ra-ma iṣ-ba-at-ni-a-tí-ma,"Aššur-ṣulūlī, son of Aššur-šād-ilī representing Kuliya, son of Ali-abum, seized us against Aššur-emūqī, son of Šu-rama,"
um-ma a-šur-DÙL-ma KÙ.BABBAR be-lúm-ba-ni DAM.GÀR-ri-im ša ku-li-a tal-qé lá tal-qé-e IGI a-ni-e-ma i-ki-ir ú-ul kà-i-in,"and Aššur-ṣulūlī said as follows: The silver of Bēlum-bāni, the agent of Kuliya, did you take it, yes or no? Deny or confirm before these men."
um-ma a-šur-e-mu-qí-ma al-qé ú al-qé-ma ú u₄-ma-am a-lá-qé-ma,"Aššur-emūqī said: I took it, yes I took it and today I would (again) take it!"
a-na a-wa-tim a-ni-a-tim kà-ru-um kà-ni-eš TUR.GAL i-dí-na-ni IGI GÍR ša a-šur ší-bu-tí a-dí-in,For this affair the plenary Kanesh 'gave' me (as witness) and before Aššur's dagger I gave my testimony.
a-šur-lá-ma-sí DUMU i-tur₄-a-num tap-pá-i,"Aššur-lamassī, son of Itūr-Anum, was my companion."
KIŠIB a-šùr-lá-ma-sí DUMU i-tur₄-a-num,"Seal of Aššur-lamassī, son of Itūr-Anum."
a-šur-DÙL DUMU a-šur-ša-dí-li ša ki-ma ku-li-a DUMU a-lá-bi₄-im a-na a-šùr-e-mu-qí DUMU šu-ra-ma iṣ-ba-at-ni-a-tí-ma,"Aššur-ṣululī, son of Aššur-šād-ilē, who represents Kuliya, son of Ali-abum, seized us against Aššur-emūqī, son of Šu-rama,"
um-ma a-šur-ANDUL-ma a-na a-šur-e-mu-qí-ma KÙ.BABBAR be-lúm-ba-ni DAM.GÀR-ri-im ša ku-li-a tal-qé lá tal-qé-e IGI a-ni-e-ma i-ki-ir ú-ul kà-i-in,"and Aššur-ṣululī said to Aššur-emūqī: Did you take the silver of Bēlum-bāni Kuliya's agent, yes or no? Deny or confirm it before these (witnesses)!"
um-ma a-šur-e-mu-qí-ma al-qé ú al-qé-ma ú u₄-ma-am a-lá-qé-ma,"Aššur-emūqī answered: I took it, yes I took it and today I would (again) take (it)!"
a-na a-wa-tim a-ni-a-tim kà-ru-um té-ga-ra-ma TUR.GAL i-dí-na-ni-ma IGI GÍR ša a-šur,For this affair the plenary of Tegarama gave us and before Aššur's dagger.
ma-la lu-qú-tum a-na a-šùr-be-el-a-wa-tim i-pí-iq-du-ma ša-lim-a-šùr ú-šé-ṣí-ú,"With regard to what goods had been entrusted to Aššur-bēl-awātim and which Šalim-Aššur had taken out,"
šu-ma a-na šu-ku-bi-im ma-ma-an i-tù-a-ar ša-lim-a-šùr ú-ba-áb-šu,"if anyone raises claim against Šu-Kūbum, Šalim-Aššur will clear him."
IGI a-šùr-ma-lik DUMU a-lá-ḫi-im IGI a-šùr-i-mì-tí DUMU i-ku-pí-IŠTAR IGI en-na-sú-in DUMU šu-IŠTAR,"Witnessed by Aššur-malik son of Ali-ahum, by Aššur-imittī son of Ikūn-pī-Ištar, by Enna-Suen son of Šu-Ištar."
