KIŠIB a-ḫu-wa-qar DUMU a-šur-SIPA,"Seal of Ahu-waqar, son of Aššur-rē'ī."
KIŠIB a-mur-a-šur DUMU šu-iš-ḫa-ra,"Seal of Amur-Aššur, son of Šu-Išhara."
KIŠIB (d)a-šur-(d)UTU-ši DUMU ili₅-ba-ni,"Seal of Aššur-šamšī, son of Ilī-bāni."
ša a-al-DU₁₀ a-na a-mur-a-šur iṣ-bu-tù-ni-a-tí,(The fact) that Āl-ṭāb seized us against Amur-Aššur.
um-ma a-al-DU₁₀-ma a-na a-mur-a-šur-ma,Āl-ṭāb said to Amur-Aššur:
K1.BABBAR a-ta ú šu-IŠTAR qá-tám mì-iš-la i-na ša ip-ṭí-ri-i ša-qá-lá-am la qá-bi₄-a-tù-nu,"""Did you and Šu-Ištar not promise to pay silver, each a half-share of the ransom?"""
um-ma a-mur-a-šur-ma ke-na qá-bi₄-a-ni ú i-na né-me-lim-x ša-li-iš-tám áš-du-na-kà i-zu-a-az ú a-na i-bi₄-sà-e ša-li-iš-tám i-za-az,"Amur-Aššur said: ""Yes, we promised, and he shall divide for you a one-third share of the profit and take a one-third share of the losses."""
KIŠIB ka-ku-a DUMU i-dí-IŠTAR,"Seal of Kakua, son of Iddin-Ištar."
KIŠIB PUZUR₄-(d)IŠKUR DUMU i-dí-IŠTAR,"Seal of Puzur-Adad, son of Iddin-Ištar."
KIŠIB na-ra-am-a-šùr DUMU ì-dí-ba-ni,"Seal of Narām-Aššur, son of Iddin-bāni."
KIŠIB ḫa-na-na DUMU DINGIR-kur-ub,"Seal of Hanana, son of Ilum-kurub."
0.33333 ma-na 5 GÍN K1.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am ša ik-ri-bi ša me-er-ú DINGIR-kur-ub i-ṣé-er en-na-sú-in DUMU a-mur-(d)UTU ir-ší-ú-ni,Enna-Suen son of Amur-Šamaš owed 1/3 mina 5 shekels of refined silver from the votive offerings of the sons of Ilum-kurub.
ki-ma me-er-e DINGIR-kur-ub K1.BABBAR ù ṣí-ba-sú ḫa-na-na ša-bu,"On behalf of the sons of Ilum-kurub, Hanana is satisfied with the silver and its interest."
ṭup-pu-um ša 0.33333 ma-na 5 GÍN K1.BABBAR ša ḫu-bu-ul en-na-sú-in ša e-li-a-ni sà-ar,"The tablet concerning 1/3 mina 5 shekels of silver, the debt of Enna-Suen, which appeared, is invalid."
šu-ma me-er-ú DINGIR-kur-ub a-na en-na-sú-in i-tù-ru-ú ḫa-na-na ú-ba-áb-šu,"If the sons of Ilum-kurub raise a claim against Enna-Suen, Hanana will clear him."
K1.BABBAR ša IGI en-na-nim ù DUMU x i-dí-nu-šu-ni,The silver which they gave him before Ennānim and the son of [X].
um-ma wa-ak-lúm-ma a-na kà-ri-im kà-ni-iš-ki qí-bí-ma,Thus says the Ruler to the Kanesh colony:
a-lu-um dì-nam IGI GIŠ.GAG-en GAL-en i-na ḫa-am-ri-im i-dí-ma,The City has passed a verdict in front of the two great pegs in the sacred precinct:
i-dí-sú-in DUMU i-ba-a-a ra-bi-ṣa-am e-ḫa-az-ma,Iddin-Suen son of Ibaya may hire an attorney.
… ša-lim-a-šùr DUMU i-sú-ri-ik [...] x x ri-im-…,... Šalim-Aššur son of Issu-arik ...
li-mu-um DINGIR-šu-GAL DUMU ba-zi-a,The eponym is Ilšu-rabi son of Baziya.
šu-ku-bu-um DUMU a-šùr-i-dí ra-bi-ṣí,Šu-Kūbum son of Aššur-idī is my attorney.
kà-ru-um dí-nam i-dí-in-ma,The colony has passed a verdict:
a-na lu-qú-tim ma-la a-na a-šùr-be-el-a-wa-tim i-pí-iq-du-ma ša-lim-a-šùr ú-šé-ṣí-ú,"Concerning all the goods that were entrusted to Aššur-bēl-awātim, and which Šalim-Aššur had taken out,"
ṭup-pá-am ša ku-nu-ki-šu ša-lim-a-šùr a-na šu-ku-bi-im i-da-an,Šalim-Aššur will give a tablet bearing his seal to Šu-Kūbum.
a-na kur-ub-IŠTAR šu-ku-bu-um ú-lá i-tù-a-ar,Šu-Kūbum will not raise a claim against Kurub-Ištar.
šu-ma a-na šu-ku-bi-im ma-ma-an i-tù-a-ar ša-lim-a-šùr ú-ba-áb-šu,"If anyone raises a claim against Šu-Kūbum, Šalim-Aššur will clear him."
um-ma tù-ra-mì-ili₅-ma a-na en-um-a-šùr ù šu-ku-bi-ma qí-bí-ma,Thus says Tūram-ilī to Ennam-Aššur and Šu-Kūbum:
35 ma-na AN.NA i li-bi a-šùr-ma-lik ù a-ḫa-ma 27 ma-na AN.NA i li-bi a-šur-ma-lik ú šu-ku-bi-im i-ba-ší,"35 minas of tin is in the possession of Aššur-malik, and also 27 minas of tin is in the possession of Aššur-malik and Šu-Kūbum."
ŠU.NÍGIN 1 GÚ 2 ma-na AN.NA,Total: 1 talent 2 minas of tin.
a-ṣé-er a-šur-ma-lik ṭí-iḫ-a-ma AN.NA lu-šé-bi-lu-nim,Approach Aššur-malik and let them send me the tin.
um-ma šu-IŠTAR-ma ù la-qé-pu-um-ma a-na tám-kà-ri-im qí-bí-ma,Thus says Šu-Ištar and Lā-qēp to the merchant:
10 ma-na K1.BABBAR ni-is-ḫa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu ku-nu-ki-kà i-dí-a-bu-um ub-lam,"Iddin-abum brought 10 minas of silver, its nishatu-tax added, its šaddu'utu-tax paid, under your seal."
ŠÀ.BA 1 GÚ 5 ma-na 6 GÍN AN.NA ku-nu-ku 15.66666 GÍN.TA K1.BABBAR-ap-šu 4 ma-na 9.33333 GÍN,"Thereof: 1 talent 5 minas 6 shekels of sealed tin at 15.666 per (shekel of silver), its silver value: 4 minas 9.333 shekels."
40 TÚG.ḫA.A ša qá-tim 2.33333 ma-na K1.BABBAR it-bu-lu,40 ordinary textiles cost 2.333 minas of silver.
15.33333 ma-na 5 GÍN AN.NA qá-tim 15 GÍN.TA K1.BABBAR-ap-šu 1 ma-na 1.66666 GÍN,"15.333 minas 5 shekels of expense-tin at 15 to 1, its silver value: 1 mina 1.666 shekels."
2 ANŠE ṣa-lá-mu 0.66666 ma-na 6 GÍN K1.BABBAR it-bu-lu,2 black donkeys cost 2/3 mina 6 shekels of silver.
0.5 ma-na K1.BABBAR be-ú-lá-at 1 sà-ri-dim i-dí-a-bu-um il₅-qé,Iddin-abum received 1/2 mina of silver as the working capital of one packer.
2 GÍN lu-bu-šu ša-bu,He was paid 2 shekels for his clothing.
5 GÍN K1.BABBAR wa-ṣí-tám ni-dí-in,We gave 5 shekels of silver for the export duty.
5 GÍN K1.BABBAR ú-nu-ut ANŠE,5 shekels of silver: harness for the donkeys.
1 GÍN ša sà-e-tim,1 shekel: for the sā'utu-tax.
K1.BABBAR ga-am-ra-kum,The silver has been spent for you.
mì-ma a-nim ku-nu-ki-ni i-dí-a-bu-um i-ra-dí-a-kum,Iddin-abum is bringing all this to you under our seals.
um-ma en-um-a-šur-ma a-na en-na-sú-in ù DINGIR-ba-ni qí-bí-ma,Thus says Ennam-Aššur to Enna-Suen and Ilī-bāni:
šál-ma-ku lu ḫa-dí-a-ni₇,"I am well, let us be glad!"
mì-ma i-ṣé-ri-a šál-ma-a-šur lá il₅-qé,Šalim-Aššur took nothing on my account.
É a-bi-ni a-na-ku ù a-tù-nu na-am-ra-ni,"As for our paternal house, I and you are happy!"
a-pu-tum tí-ib-a-ni-ma a-tal-kà-nim,Urgent: set out and come!
1 GÍN K1.BABBAR ší-tám ša DINGIR-ba-ni en-na-sú-in ub-lam,"Enna-Suen brought 1 shekel of silver, the remainder belonging to Ilī-bāni."
ša i-na-sú-in LUGAL-(d)IM mì-ma lá ub-lam,Šar-Adad has not brought anything belonging to Enna-Suen.
ù šu-ma be-ú-lá-at-ku-nu ba-at-qá-tù-nu a-na-ku ú-ša-ba,"Also, if you are in arrears with your working capitals, I shall pay (them)."
iš-tí a-ba-ba ta-ma-ku,I have sworn together with Ababa.
i-sú-rik₁₃ a-na a-lim(ki) i-lá-ak-ma,"As Issu-arik will go to the City,"
É-tí-šu ša bu-ri-im a-šar a-ni-i ša-lim-a-šùr wa-áš-bu-ni a-na tù-ud-ḫa-li-a a-ḫu tù-li a-na ší-mì-im i-dí-šu-nu,"he sold his houses by the well, where at present Šalim-Aššur is living, to Tudhaliya the brother of Tuli."
a-na a-wa-tim a-ni-a-tim kà-ru-um kà-ni-iš i-dí-ni-a-tí-ma,The Kanesh colony gave us (verdict) for these proceedings.
ṭup-pá-am ší-bu-tí-ni IGI GÍR ša a-šùr ni-dí-in,We gave a tablet with our testimony before the dagger of Aššur.
IGI sú-kà-li-a DUMU a-mur-a-šùr,Witnessed by Sukkalliya son of Amur-Aššur.
IGI a-ku-za DUMU šu-a-nim,Witnessed by Akuza son of Šu-Anum.
IGI ú-ra-a DUMU ma-na na,Witnessed by Uraya son of Manana.
3 GÍN K1.BABBAR i li-bi ku-ku-lá-nim,3 shekels of silver is owed by Kukkulānum.
a-ḫa-ma 0.75 GÍN K1.BABBAR šu-ut-ma …,"Also, 3/4 shekel of silver is (owed by) him ..."
14 mu-ta-tim 2 e-li-ta-an ku-nu-ku ša šé-ep-IŠTAR ù ša-lim-wa-ardí,14 half-packs and 2 top-packs sealed by Šēp-Ištar and Šalim-wardī.
a-na DAM (d)IŠTAR-pí-lá-ah šé-ep-IŠTAR ù ša-lim-wa-ardí ip-qídu,Šēp-Ištar and Šalim-wardī entrusted them to the wife of Ištar-pilah.
IGI i-dí-a-šùr DUMU ku-zi-lá-nim,Witnessed by Iddin-Aššur son of Kuzilānum.
IGI DU₁₀-a-hi-e DUMU ir-bi₄-(d)IM x x-mu-ta-bi₄-il₅,"Witnessed by Ṭāb-ahe, son of Irbi-Adad, and ...-muttabbil."
IGI PUZUR₄-ša-du-e a-hi a-lá-hi-im,Witnessed by Puzur-šadu’e brother of Ali-ahum.
um-ma ša-qí-il₅ da-tim ku-li-a ší-ip-ru-um ša kà-ri-im kà-ni-iš ù kà-ru-um dur₄-hu-mì-it-ma a-na kà-ar kà-ar-ma ù wa-ba-ra-tim a-dí kà-ri-im kà-ni-iš qí-bi-ma,"Thus say the 'datu-payers,' Kuliya, the messenger of Kanesh, and the colony of Durhumit: speak to every single colony and trading station until the colony of Kanesh."
a-sá-num ší-pár-ni a-na ta-i-tim a-na kà-ri-im kà-ni-iš ša-pí-ir,"Asānum, our messenger, has been sent to the Kanesh colony to deliver information."
a-pu-tum ki-ma tup-pí-ni ta-áš-me-a-ni iš-té-na mu-qá-ri-bé a-na a-sá-num dí-na-ma,"Please, as soon as you have heard our letter, give an escort to Asānum."
kà-ru-um kà-ri-im a-dí kà-ni-iš(ki) lu-qá-ri-bu-šu,"Each colony must escort him to the next, all the way until Kanesh."
u₄-ma-kàl lá i-sà-hur,He must not suffer a delay of even one single day!
a-na a-la-hi-im qí-bi₄-ma um-ma ha-nu-ma,"To Ali-ahum speak, thus says Hanu:"
a ma-lá tí-ir-tí-kà šu-hu-bu-ur ù a-na-ku ni-zi-iz-ma a-lu-lá-a ni-iṣ-ba-at-ma um-ma né-nu-ma,"In accordance with your instructions, Šu-hubur and I stood up and we seized Alulaya and said:"
