um-ma a-lu-lá-a-ma KÙ.BABBAR iš-tù ITU.1.KAM bur-sú-in ú-šé-bi₄-il₅-šu-um,"Alulaya answered: ""I sent the silver to him a month ago with Būr-Suen."""
a-dí ta-ah-sí-is-tim ša tù-ša-hi-zi-ni a-lu-lá-a a-áš-al-šu-ma um-ma šu-ut-ma,"With respect to the memorandum that you instructed me about, I questioned Alulaya, and he answered:"
la-qé-pum DUMU šu-ašur ú-kà-al-ší,"""Lā-qēpum son of Šu-Aššur has it."""
ù a-hu-wa-qar DUMU zu-ur-zu-ur a-áš-al-ma um-ma šu-ut-ma,"I also questioned Ahu-waqar son of Zurzur, and he answered:"
ta-ah-sí-is-tám ili₅-ba-ni DUMU ba-ší-li ú-kà-al-ší,"""Ilī-bāni son of Baši-ilī has the memorandum."""
a-zu aṣ-ba-at-ma um-ma šu-ut-ma,I seized Azu and he answered:
ki ma-ṣí lu KÙ.BABBAR lu pì-ri-kà-ni-kà 5 GÍN.TA a-lá-qé,"""I shall take enough, either in silver or from your pirikannu-textiles at 5 shekels per piece."""
um-ma šu-ut-ma ba-áb ha-ra-ni-kà KÙ.BABBAR ú ṣí-ba-sú a-kà-na-kà-ma,"He said further: ""At the start of your journey I shall seal the silver and its interest for you."""
a-dí ší-li-ip-kà-im šu-kà-tám aṣ-ba-at-ma um-ma šu-ut-ma ší-li-ip-kà-um i-ba-ší,"Regarding the šilipka’um-textile I seized Šukkutum, and he answered: ""The šilipka’um is available."""
a-dí-ni-ma be-lí a-ta a-ma-kam tù-na-hi-da-ni um-ma a-ta-ma a-na u₄-me-šu ú-šé-ra-kum,"It still is, and you cautioned me there, my lord, saying: ""I have released them to you for its term."""
u₄-ma-am ta-áš-ta-na-me ki-ma ší-mu-um kà-sú,Today you keep hearing that trade is at a standstill.
ší-mì a-da-ma a-ta-be-a-ma a-ta-lá-kam,"I shall sell my goods, set out and come."
ki-ma me-er-e šál-ma-a-šur a-na qá-ta-tim a-da-ku-nu,Representing the sons of Šalim-Aššur I hand you over to guarantors.
me-er-ú me-tim né-nu,We are inheritors (sons of a dead man).
tup-pá-am ša ša-lá-ša-at a-tù-nu ha-bu-lá-tù-nu-ni-ma KÙ.BABBAR i qá-qá-ad šál-mì-ku-nu ra-ak-sú nu-kà-al,We have in our possession a tablet stating that you three owe silver and that you are jointly liable.
lu ša pá-e a-na ša-lim-a-šur tí-šu,"If you have oral witnesses against Šalim-Aššur,"
lu a-na a-ba-e-ni tí-šu-ú,"or if you have some against our fathers,"
lu tup-pá-am ša ša-ba-e ša ku-nu-uk a-ba-e-ni tù-kà-al,"or if you hold a tablet of satisfaction with the seal of our fathers,"
lu ší-be-e tí-šu,"or if you have witnesses,"
a-na a-né-en-ma ru-a-ma mì-nam ni-qá-bi₄,"then produce the evidence to these men, and what can we then say?"
me-er-ú me-tim né-nu lá tù-ba-ar-ni-a-tí,We are inheritors. Do not drag us to court.
i-na 4 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša hu-bu-ul PUZUR₄-(d)EN.LÍL ša tup-pí-šu ha-ar-mì-im ù 0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša a-ha-ma a-dí-šu-ni ŠÀ.BA 4.5 GÚ 4.5 ma-na URUDU al-qé,"Of the 4 minas of silver that are the debt of Puzur-Enlil, recorded in his certified tablet, and of the 0.5 mina of silver I had given him separately, thereof I obtained 4.5 talents 4.5 minas of copper."
i-na 1 GÚ 50 ma-na URUDU ù 10 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša hu-bu-ul PUZUR₄-(d)EN.LÍL ŠÀ.BA 1 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR KI ša-lim-a-šùr DUMU up-ha-qí-im aṣ-ba-at,"Of the 1 talent 50 minas of copper and 10 shekels of silver that are the debt of Puzur-Enlil, thereof I seized 1 mina of silver from Šalim-Aššur, son of Uphāqum."
i-na 4 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša na-pá-hu iš-qú-lu-ni-ni 0.83333 ma-na 3.33333 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ma-sú-ha-am qá-dum 3.33333 GÍN mu-ṭá-e i-na li-bi-šu-nu a-hu-ur,"Of the 4 minas of silver that the smiths paid to me, 0.83333 mina 3.3333 shekels of silver of inferior quality together with 3.3333 shekels underweight remain as owed by them."
ŠÀ.BA 0.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR a-na PUZUR₄-a-šur ša šu-ì-lí-a áš-qúl,Thereof I paid 0.5 mina of silver to Puzur-Aššur of Šu-Iliya.
2 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša ší-im AN.NA-ki-kà ša i-na tí-me-el-ki-a al-qé-ú,2 minas of silver from the proceeds on your tin which I received in Timelkiya.
10.33333 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša a be-a-lim ta-dí-nu-šu-ni a-na šé-ep-IŠTAR a-dí-in,"I gave 10.33333 shekels of silver, which you gave him for use, to Šēp-Ištar."
5.5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a-na sà-áp-tí-nim a-na am-tí-kà a-dí-in,I gave 5.5 shekels of silver for a saptinnu-textile to your maid-servant.
x x x x x x TÚG SIG₅ i-na x hu-ra-ma a-dí-na-ku-um,... fine textile in ... Hurama I gave to you.
5.25 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša a-šu-mì šé-ep-IŠTAR a qá-tí-kà tù-ṭá-hi-ú,5.25 shekels of silver which you added to your share on account of Šēp-Ištar.
2 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša a-na a-bu-a áš-qú-lu-ni,2 shekels of silver which I paid to my father.
0.66666 ma-na 5 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR a-na ir-i-bi₄-im áš-qúl,I paid 0.66666 mina 5 shekels of silver to Ir-ibum.
5 ma-na AN.NA ù 3 ku-ta-ni i li-bi₄-kà i-šu,I have a claim of 5 minas of tin and 3 kutānu-textiles against you.
a-ba-ba ra-bi-ṣú-um ša É ša-lim-a-šur en-um-a-šur ù ṣí-li-a ša ki-ma a-la-hi-im a-na i-dí-a-šùr iṣ-ba-at-ni-a-tí-ma um-ma a-ba-ba ra-bi-ṣú-ma a-na i-dí-a-šùr-ma,"Ababa, the attorney of Šalim-Aššur's firm, Ennam-Aššur and Ṣilliya, Ali-ahum's representative, seized us against Iddin-Aššur and the attorney Ababa said to Iddin-Aššur:"
tup-pá-am ša a-lim(ki) ta-áš-me,You have heard the tablet from the City.
KÙ.BABBAR-ap ša-lim-a-šur ú-pá-ha-ar,I collect Šalim-Aššur's silver;
ù na-áš-pé-er-tám ša um-me-a-ni ša-lim-a-šur iš-tù ITU.KAM hu-bu-ur li-mì-im a-šur-ma-lik DUMU a-lá-hi-im ub-lá-kum ša 40 GÚ URUDU SIG₅ ip-qí-du-ni-ku-ni tù-šé-ra-am,"also, I brought you a missive from Šalim-Aššur's investors from the month Hubur, eponymy of Aššur-malik son of Ali-ahum, stating that you must release 40 talents of good copper that they entrusted to you,"
ù a-na me-er-e ša-lim-a-šur la ta-tù-ar,and you must not raise claim against Šalim-Aššur's sons.
40 GÚ URUDU SIG₅ ša um-me-a-ni ša-lim-a-šur ta-pu-lu-ni a-na ma-lá na-áš-pè-er-tí-šu-nu iš-tù ITU.1.KAM hu-bu-ur li-mu-um a-šur-ma-lik DUMU a-lá-hi-im URUDU al-qé,"I have received the 40 talents of good copper about which you reached an agreement with Šalim-Aššur's investors, in accordance with their missive dated month Hubur, eponymy Aššur-malik son of Ali-ahum."
lá tù-na-ha-ni,Do not obstruct me.
a-ma a-wi-lu a-ni-ú-tum lu i-de₈-ú,"Indeed, may these men know!"
na-áš-pé-er-tám ša um-me-a-ni IGI a-ni-ú-tim ší-me-ma a-na me-er-e ša-lim-a-šur lá ta-tù-ar,"Listen to the missive from the investors before these witnesses, and do not raise claim against Šalim-Aššur's sons."
… ma-lá ga-me-er a-wa-tí-ni …,... as much as those who settled our case ...
i-na na-áš-pè-er-tí-šu-nu … ú-ša-hi-it-kà,I have cleared you with their missive.
i-dí-a-šur ra-bi₄-ṣa-am ša É ša-lim-a-šur en-um-a-šur ù ṣí-li-a ša,"Iddin-Aššur answered the attorney of Šalim-Aššur's firm, Ennam-Aššur and Ṣilliya."
5 ma-na hu-ša-e i-na kà-ṣí-im a-na ta-ší-a-tim,5 minas of scrap (copper) in the steppe for transport.
iš-tù qá-ṭá-ra a-dí ha-mì-za-nim 0.33333-ma-na AN.NA a-ta-ší-a-tim,From Qaṭṭarā until hamizānum 0.3333 mina of tin for transport.
ANŠE uš-pá-il₅-ma 1-ma-na 15 GÍN AN.NA a-pu-ul,I replaced a donkey and had to balance 1 mina and 15 shekels of tin.
