ITU.1.KAM ṣí-ip-um li-mu-um PUZUR₄-(d)MUŠ,"Month VII, eponymy of Puzur-Nirah."
šu-ma i-na ša 10 TÚG-tum 1 TÚG wa-at-ru-ú-tim i-na É.GAL-lim il₅-qé-ŠU ki-iš-dá-tí-šu a-na e-lá-ma i-na TÚG.ḪI-tí-šu i-ṣa-bi-ir-šum ša ILLAT la-qé-ep DUMU qá-a-a-tim,"If one has taken extra pieces in the palace, on top of the tithe on textiles, what accrues from it to Elamma will be deducted for him from his textiles of the caravan of Lā-qēp, son of Qa'atum."
IGI i-dí-a-šur DUMU bu-sú-sú IGI a-bu-ša-lim DUMU i-dí-èr-ra,"In the presence of Iddin-Aššur, son of Pususu, of Abu-šalim, son of Iddin-Erra."
a-na i-ku-pí-a li-bi-IŠTAR a-lá-ḫi-im ù a-šur-ma-lik a-na li-bi-IŠTAR qí-bi-ma um-ma PUZUR₄-a-na-ma,"To Ikūn-pīya, Libbi-Ištar, Ali-ahum and Aššur-malik; specifically to Libbi-Ištar from Puzur-Anna:"
3 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ni-is-ḫa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu ša DAM.GÀR-ri-im a-dí-na-kum,"I gave you 3 minas of silver, its import duty added, its transport tariff paid for, belonging to a merchant."
i-na a-wa-tí-ni ší-a-ma-at a-lim(ki) lu 1 ma-na-um 0.66666 ma-na lu 1 ma-na-um 0.5 ma-na a-na DAM.GÀR-ri-im ta-da-an,According to our agreement you will give from the purchase in the City either 0.6666 mina or 0.5 mina per mina to the merchant.
ù a-ta 4 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ni-is-ḫa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu i-a-tí ki-ma DAM.GÀR ta-da-nam-ma ù a-na-ku DAM.GÀR-ru-um i-na e-la-i-a-ma iš-tù a-lim(ki) a-da-na-kum,"Then, you will personally give 4 minas of silver, its import duty added, its transport tariff paid for, to me, on behalf of the merchant, and then I shall personally be the merchant; when I come up (to Anatolia) from the City I shall give it to you."
a-ḫi a-ta KÙ.BABBAR ù ší-a-ma-tim KÙ.BABBAR ma-la ta-na-dí-ú a-na ša ki-ma i-a-tí dí-in,"My dear brother, give whatever silver and purchases you will deposit to my representatives."
ù a-ta 4 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ni-is-ḫa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu šé-bi₄-lam-ma KÙ.BABBAR ma-la a-ta ta-da-na-ni ù a-na-ku i-na e-lá-i-a ki-am la-dí-na-kum,"Also, you must personally send me 4 minas of silver, its import duty added, its transport tariff paid for, and whatever silver you give to me I shall personally give to you in this way when I come up."
šu-ma ší-ma-am i-da-na-ku-nu-tí la ta-ma-ḫa-ra-šu ù tí-ir-ta-ku-nu li-li-kam,"If he gives you purchased goods, do not receive them but send me word."
um-ma ku-zi-zi-a-ma ù a-mur-IŠTAR-ma a-na a-lá-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma,From Kuziziya and Amur-Ištar to Ali-ahum:
i-na 15 TÚG ša a-mur-IŠTAR e-zi-bu iš-tù a-mur-IŠTAR i-tù-ra-ni 2 TÚG i-ni-id-nu,Of the 15 textiles that Amur-Ištar left behind two textiles have been sold after Amur-Ištar returned.
4 TÚG ša a-bi-a-nu-um ú-šé-bi-lá-ni ú 4 TÚG ku-a-ú-tim ŠU.NÍGIN 8 TÚG i li-bi-a,4 textiles that Abī-Anum sent and your own 4 textiles: in all 8 textiles are in my possession.
mì-šu ša a-na 6 TÚG.ḪI.A ša a-bi-a-nim ša ta-áš-pu-ra-ni a-lá-an 4 TÚG ša ú-šé-bi₄-lá-ni mì-ma wa-at-ra-am lá ú-šé-bi₄-lam,"Why is it that as for the 6 textiles belonging to Abī-Anum that you wrote about, apart from the 4 textiles he sent he has not sent anything else?"
ù a-dí-ni 2 TÚG ší-ma-sú i-ba-ší-ú,"So, until now the 2 textiles agreed by him are (still) outstanding."
a-ma-kam a-lu-a ša-il₅ ša TÚG.ḪI.A ub-lá-ni ší-im 4 TÚG ša a-bi-A-nim ú ší-im ku-a-ú-tim,"Ask Aluwa there, who brought the textiles, about the price of Abī-Anum's 4 textiles and that of yours."
šu-ma a-we-lu i-na sí-kà-tim wa-áš-bu i-na e-ra-bi-šu-nu lu … lu SÍG-tim e-ba-… ú-šé-ba-lá-kum,"If the men are staying in the sikkātum, then when they arrive I shall send you both ... and the wool ..."
… TÚG.ḪI-tí-kà 12 … i-na ku-nu-uk … be-lúm-ba-ni i-ba-ší-ú,... of your 12 textiles ... are present under Bēlum-bāni's seal.
i-na TÚG.ḪI.A a-ni-ú-tim mì-ma a-mur-IŠTAR ú-lá il₅-qé,Amur-Ištar has not taken any of these textiles.
3 kà-sà-tum ù tù-dí-na-tum šu-qú-ul-ta-áš-na 1 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu-ku-a,"3 cups and toggle pins, their weight in silver 1 mina, under my seals;"
a-ḫa-ma 0.33333 ma-na 6 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ku-nu-ku-a-ma ik-ri-bu ša e-lá-ma,"separately 26 shekels of silver also under my seals, of Elamma;"
2 ṭup-pu-ú ša 2 ma-na 15 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša ḫu-bu-ul nu-a-im,"2 tablets of 2 minas 15 shekels of silver, being in the debt of the Anatolian;"
1 ṭup-pu-um ša 1.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša ḫu-bu-ul na-ni-a,"1 tablet of 1.5 mina of silver, being the debt of Naniya;"
1 ṭup-pu-um ša 1 ma-na 6 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša ḫu-bu-ul bur-sú-en₆,"1 tablet of 1 mina and 6 shekels of silver, being the debt of Būr-Suen;"
1 ṭup-pu-um ša 0.33333 ma-na 4 GÍN KÙ.BABBAR ša ḫu-bu-ul il₅-tap-pá,1 tablet of 24 shekels of silver being the debt of Ilī-tappā;
1 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR a-na ir-ma-a-šùr a-na ší-a-ma-tim a-dí-in,1 mina of silver (that) I gave to Ir'am-Aššur for making purchases;
1 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR a-na aḫ-ša-lim a-na ší-a-ma-tim a-dí-in,1 mina of silver (that) I gave to Ah-šalim for making purchases.
9 (TÚG)pí-ri-kà-ni ù 1 (TÚG)a-bar-ni-am a-na pí-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR a-na ší-a-ma-tim a-d-in,"9 -textiles and 1 Abarnian one, (which) I gave to Pilah-Ištar for making purchases."
5 ÌR-du ù 5 a-ma-tum ŠÀ.BA 1 am-tum i-a-an-tal-ga ša ì-lí-na DUMU.SAL a-šur-DU₁₀,"5 slaves and 5 slave-girls, of whom 1 slave-girl, named Iyantalga, is for Ilina, daughter of Aššur-ṭāb."
mì-ma a-nim lá-ma-sà-tum DAM e-lá-ma té-zi-ib,"All this, Lamassutum, the wife of Elamma, left behind."
IŠTAR-pá-lil₅ en-na-sú-en₆ ù ma-ṣí-ì-lí ša ki-ma lá-ma-sà-tum a-na DUMU um-mì-a-nim ù ma-ri-ša i-pá-qí-du-ma a-na a-lim(ki) ú-bu-lu-ú-ma,"Ištar-pālil, Ennam-Suen and Maṣi-ilī, Lamassutum's representative(s), will entrust it to an affiliated trader and to her sons and they will bring it to the City"
a ma-lá ší-ma-tí-šu-nu me-er-i-tí NIN.DINGIR,"and (there) my daughter, the priestess, and my sons will act in accordance with the testamentary dispositions applying to them."
2 ší-ta sà-ma-lá-tim ra-bi₄-a-tim a-… ša ba-áb ni x … a-dí-šum,2 big -cups ... of the gate ... I gave to him.
0.5 GÍN …,½ shekel...
4 sà-ma-lá-tim … lá i-ḫa-li-qú …,4 -cups ... should not be lost.
a-na (d)IM-ba-ni … Ì-lí-iš-ta-ki-il₅ … ù pí-la-aḫ-IŠTAR qí-bi-ma um-ma DAM.GÀR-um-ma,"To Adad-bāni ..., Iliš-takil ... and Pilah-Ištar from the merchant:"
1 GÚ 35 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ni-is-ḫa-sú DIRI ša-du-a-sú ša-bu-ú pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR ù ú-zu-a na-áš-a-ku-nu-tí,"Pilah-Ištar and Uzuwa bring you 1 talent 35 minas of silver, its import duty added, its transport tariff paid for."
a-ḫu-a a-tù-nu ú iḫ-da-ma AN.NA-kam da-am-qám wa-at-ra-am ma-ḫi-ir i-za-zu x ú ba šu … ša-a-ma šu-uq-lam-…,"My dear brothers, buy tin of extra-fine quality according to the market price and ..."
x KÙ.GI pá-ša-lam da-am-qám ša ba-ri-ni pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR na-áš-a-ku-nu-ti,Pilah-Ištar brings you x fine -gold belonging to us jointly.
a-ḫu-a a-tù-nu ú iḫ-da-ma KI pá-ni-im wa-ṣí-im lu-qú-ti áb-kà-nim,"My dear brothers, dispatch my goods with the first leaving caravan."
ú a-ḫa-ma 40 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am ša a-na šu-mì É a-bi₄-a a-na pì-lá-aḫ-IŠTAR áp-qí-id,"Also, I further entrusted 40 minas of refined silver in the name of our father's house to Pilah-Ištar."
IGI pu-šu-ki-in IGI ku-zi-zi-a IGI (d)IM-re-x,"Witnessed by Pūšu-kēn, by Kuziziya, by Adad-rē'ī."
um-ma en-nam-a-šur-ma a-na a-la-ḫi-im qí-bi-ma,From Ennam-Aššur to Ali-ahum:
a-na-kam a-du um-me-a-an a-bi-ni a-we-lu-ú 2 ší-na im-ta-ag-ru-ni mì-ša-al KÙ.BABBAR ma-ḫri-šu a-šà-kà-an-ma a-na a-lim(ki) ší-ni-šu i-lá-ak-ma KÙ.BABBAR-pí-šu-nu uš-ta-bu-ú,"Here 2 men have reached an agreement with me concerning our father's investors, that I shall place half of the silver before him, and it will go twice to the City and they will satisfy themselves with their silver."
a-du-um 3.5 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ša i-na a-lim(ki) a-bu-ni i-ṣé-er ú-ṣur-ša-IŠTAR il₅-qé-ú a ší-a-tí kà-áb-sà-ni,Concerning 3.5 minas of silver that our father took on Uṣur-ša-Ištar's account in the City - for that we are pardoned.
a-wa-tum i-ma-qú-ut-ma a-dí 5 u₄-me-e … ú e-ma-ri iš-tí … a-ṭá-ra-dam,"The matter will fail, and within 5 days ... and I shall send the donkeys with ..."
ú a-ta-ma a-ma-kam lu za-ku-a-tí,Then you too must be cleared there.
URUDU lá-mu-nam a-na SIG₅ ta-e-er,Convert bad copper to good.
a-pu-tum ša ša-ni-ú-tim la ta-áš-ta-na-me-e,Urgent! Do not listen to others all the time.
mì-šu ša áš-ta-na-me-ú-ma a-wa-at a-ḫi-ú-tim ta-áš-ta-na-me-ú,Why is it that I keep hearing that you always listen to what strangers say?
a-pu-tum la ta-ša-lá-at,Urgent! Do not act rashly.
3 ma-na KÙ.BABBAR ṣa-ru-pá-am i-na ší-im SÍG.ḪI.A ša ú-ší-na-lam i-lá-áš-ra-ni DUMU sú-kà-li-a il₅-qé,Ilī-ašrannī son of Sukkalliya has received 3 minas of refined silver from the proceeds of Ušinalam's wool.
IGI a-šùr-ba-ni DUMU kur-bi-a-a IGI iš-me-DINGIR IGI i-dí-ku-bi-im,"Witnessed by Aššur-bāni son of Kurbiya, by Išme-ilum, by Iddin-Kūbum."
ša-lim-a-šùr a-na a-mur-IŠTAR ú-ṭá-bi-ni-a-tí-ma um-ma ša-lim-a-šùr-ma,Šalim-Aššur made us approach Amur-Ištar and Šalim-Aššur said:
mì-šu-um ší-im 10 (TÚG)ku-ta-ni ša kà-ru-um dur₄-ḫu-mì-it a-dí-nu tal-qé,"""Why have you taken the proceeds from 10 kutānu-textiles that I sold in the Durhumit colony?"""
um-ma a-mur-IŠTAR-ma ke-na 4 GÚ URUDU lá-mu-na-am al-qé,"Amur-Ištar said: ""Yes, I have taken 4 talents of copper of poor quality."""
um-ma ša-lim-a-šùr-ma ú-lá a-kà-lá-ma ta-al-qé,"Šalim-Aššur said: ""I hold nothing, yet you have taken it."""
um-ma a-mur-IŠTAR-ma a-ta-ba lu-qú-tí lá ta-aṣ-ba-at,"Amur-Ištar said: ""It is not you who have taken my merchandise?"""
um-ma ša-lim-a-šùr-ma mì-ma lu-qú-ut-kà ú-lá aṣ-ba-at,"Šalim-Aššur answered: ""I have taken none of your merchandise."""
um-ma a-mur-IŠTAR-ma qá-i ÌR li-li-kam,"Amur-Ištar then said: ""Wait until the slave has come here."""
um-ma ša-lim-a-šùr-ma ma li-li-kam i-na pí-i ÌR-dí-kà-ma i-a-tí ta-a-bi-ta-ni,"Šalim-Aššur said: ""Sure, let him come. Then it will be me you can pressure on the basis of what your own slave says."""
lu qá-i,"""Do wait!"""
um-ma ša-lim-a-šùr-ma ù KÙ.BABBAR ša a-šu-mì i-dí-a-bi₄-im ša ta-al-qé-ú ṭup-pá-am ḫa-ar-ma-am ú-kà-lu,"Šalim-Aššur continued: ""And for the silver that you have taken concerning Iddin-abum I hold the certified tablet."""
lu a-ḫu-ra,"""That remains."""
IGI ú-ra-a IGI (d)MAR.TU-ba-ni bu-zu-ta-a tap-pá-i-ni,"Witnessed by Uraya, by Amurrum-bāni; Buzutaya was our (absent) partner."
a-na en-nam-a-šùr qí-bi-ma um-ma IŠTAR-ra-bi₄-at-ma,To Ennam-Aššur from Ištar-rabi'at:
a-dí KÙ.BABBAR-pí-kà ša ḫa-bu-lá-ku-ni DUMU a-ta li-ba-kà lá i-pá-ri-id,"With respect to your silver that I owe you, my dear son, do not worry!"
um-ma a-na-ku-ma ma-té-e ṣí-lá-(d)IM lá-mì-id,"I said: ""When will Ṣill-Adad be informed?"""
a-ta ṣí-lá-(d)IM u₄-mì-im ṣú-ḫa-ri ša i-šu-ú lá ṣú-ḫa-ru-kà,As for you - thinking of Ṣill-Adad - are not the servants I have to-day (also) your servants?
a-dí e-ṭí-i ḫa-ra-nim ṣú-ba-tí-a ú-za-kà-ma KÙ.BABBAR-áp-kà a ni-ir-tí-kà ú-qá-ra-áb,When the road (opens) I shall clear my textiles and have your silver delivered directly to your person.
a-na-kam ki-a-am ša ki-ma ku-a-tí i-zi-zu-ma a-dí li-bi-kà lu-qú-tám ù e-ma-re-e qá-at-kà ša-ki-in,"Here your representatives acted like this, so for as long as you wish your claim has been placed on the goods and the donkeys."
1 ṭup-pu-um ša be-lúm-ba-ni DUMU na-ra-am-ZU ù ší-na ṭup-pè ša DAM.GÀR ša É-tí-kà a-bi-a-nu-um e-zi-bu,"As for the tablet concerning Bēlum-bāni son of Narām-Sīn and two tablets concerning customers, which Abī-Anum left in your house,"
i-na a-lá-ak ṣú-ḫa-ri ṭup-pè lu-šé-tí-qú,when the servants arrive they will transport the tablets.
i-a-am a-dí KÙ.BABBAR-pí-kà li-ba-kà lá i-pá-ri-id,As for mine - do not worry about your silver.
1.8333300000000001 ma-na 3.5 G␀␀N K␀␀.BABBAR a-š␀r-na-da DUMU er-nu-id,"1 mina 53.5 shekels of silver with Aššur-nādā, son of Ernu'id."
0.5 ma-na 3.5 G␀␀N K␀␀.BABBAR b␀␀-␀␀-l␀␀-at a-š␀r-i-m␀␀-t␀␀ DUMU ␀␀a-la-bi-im,"33.5 shekels of silver, working capital of Aššur-imittĥ, son of Halabum."
0.33333 ma-na 5 G␀␀N K␀␀.BABBAR b␀␀-␀␀-l␀␀-at gal-da-a,"25 shekels of silver, working capital of Galdaya."
1 ma-na K␀␀.BABBAR KI gal-da-a iš-t␀␀ ITU.1.KAM ␀␀␀-ip-im 1.5 G␀␀N.TA i-na ITU.1.KAM ␀␀-␀␀a-␀␀b li-mu-um a-bi-a DUMU šu-da-g␀␀n,"1 mina of silver with Galdaya, from month VII he will add 1.5 shekel per month, eponymy of Abiya son of Šu-Dagan."
0.83333 ma-na 0.66666 G␀␀N K␀␀.BABBAR KI i-d␀␀-a-š␀r ša na-a␀␀ri-a,50.6666 shekels of silver due from Iddin-Aššur of Nahriya.
1.5 G␀␀N.TA a-na 1 ma-na-im ␀␀-␀␀a-␀␀b,He will add 1.5 shekel per mina (as interest).
0.83333 ma-na 5 G␀␀N K␀␀.BABBAR KI bur-s␀␀-in,55 shekels of silver with BŦr-Suen.
48 ma-na URUDU KI ␀␀a-ab-t␀␀-ni-␀␀š,48 minas of copper with Habtuniš.
1 ma-na 15 G␀␀N K␀␀.BABBAR ša-lim-a-šur DUMU up-␀␀ba-q␀␀-im,"1 mina 15 shekels (with) Šalim-Aššur, son of Uphāqum."
2 G␀␀ 13 ma-na URUDU KI DINGIR-ba-ni DUMU ib-ni-l␀␀,"2 talents 13 minas of copper with Ilĥ-bāni, son of Ibni-ilĥ."
0.83333 ma-na K␀␀.BABBAR KI a-š␀r-ba-ni DUMU su-ku-ku,"0.83333 mina of silver with Aššur-bāni, son of Sukkuku."
8.5 ma-na K␀␀.BABBAR KI šu-li DUMU i-li-li iš-t␀␀ ITU.1.KAM na-ar-ma-ak-a-šur 1.5 G␀␀N.TA a-na 1 ma-na-im ␀␀-␀␀a-␀␀b li-mu-um šu-IŠTAR k␀␀-␀␀b-k␀␀-ba-nu-um,"8.5 minas of silver with Šuli, son of Ellil-ilĥ, from month II/III he will add 1.5 shekel per mina, eponymy of Šu-Ištar."
1.3333300000000001 ma-na K␀␀.BABBAR KI a-š␀r-du-ri,1.3333 minas of silver with Aššur-dŦrĥ.
5 G␀␀ URUDU KI i-d␀␀-MAR.TU DUMU šu-␀␀bi-nim,"5 talents of copper with Iddin-Amurrum, son of Šuhanum."
1 ma-na K␀␀.BABBAR KI DINGIR-šu-GAL DUMU bu-l␀␀-li,"1 mina of silver with Ilšu-rabi, son of Bulāli."
a-na ku-ku-a en-na-s␀␀-in ␀␀ ␀␀-␀␀␀␀-ur-ša-a-šur q␀␀-b␀␀-ma um-ma šu-IŠTAR-ma,"Say to Kukua, Ennam-Suen and Uထur-ša-Aššur, thus Šu-Ištar:"
a-ma-kam a-am-t␀␀m s␀␀-ni-q␀␀-ma i-na ␀␀-zi-ni-im e t␀␀-pu-␀␀š-ma nu-a-am e ta-al-pu-ut,Keep the maid there under control and let her not operate in Uzinum and not affect the native Anatolian.
a-ni-ša-am ta-␀␀š-pu-ra-am um-ma š␀␀-it-ma šu-up-ra-ma š␀␀-me-a ma-ma-an li-il₅-q␀␀,She wrote me here as follows: 'Send (somebody) to collect the price due to me'.
a-␀␀bu-a-t␀␀-nu a-ma-kam am-t␀␀m s␀␀-ni-q␀␀-ma ␀␀ s␀␀-li-a-š␀␀-ma,"My dear colleagues, keep the maid there under control and cheat her:"
um-ma a-t␀␀-nu-ma a-na ␀␀␀␀-er be-li-ki-i i-ra-de₈-␀␀-ki,(tell her) as follows: 'One will conduct you to your lord.'
lu s␀␀-␀␀be-er-t␀␀-ki lu K␀␀.BABBAR 1 G␀␀N t␀␀-šu-i p␀␀-␀␀bi-ri-ma,Collect your small goods and any silver you have.
KI a-li-ki-im p␀␀-ni-ma a-na ␀␀␀␀-er be-li-ki-i ta-li-ki,And then you will go to your lord with the first caravan.
a-na-ma t␀␀-p␀␀-␀␀bu-ru-ni ␀␀␀␀-ba-s␀␀-a ␀␀ ša q␀␀-q␀␀-d␀␀-ša-a eၠ-ra-ma,And as soon as she is gathering her belongings deprive her of her garment and her head-dress.
a-na ta-al-␀␀ba-t␀␀-i-im d␀␀-na-š␀␀,Sell her to somebody from Talhat.
a-na DUMU a-š␀␀r ␀␀ DUMU k␀␀-n␀␀-eš l␀␀ ta-d␀␀-š␀␀,Do not sell her to an Assyrian or to a citizen of Kanesh.
␀␀a-li-q␀␀-␀␀š ␀␀ ma-at k␀␀-n␀␀-eš l␀␀ i-na-mar,Get rid of her and she shall never (again) be seen in the land of Kanesh.
um-ma a-šur-UTU-ši-ma a-na en-nam-a-šur q␀␀-bi-ma,From Aššur-šamšĥ to Ennam-Aššur:
